WEBVTT


00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:55.086
Happy Thanksgiving!


00:02:02.699 --> 00:02:04.237
- Here!
- Right here!


00:02:10.318 --> 00:02:11.879
Here you go, fellas!


00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.719
Come! Come here.


00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.658
This is the problem.


00:02:37.502 --> 00:02:39.557
This is what's wrong with America.


00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.635
It's gotten so big


00:02:41.964 --> 00:02:43.891
you just can't find your way.


00:02:44.551 --> 00:02:45.792
The grocery store


00:02:46.086 --> 00:02:48.233
on the corner is a now a supermarket.


00:02:48.514 --> 00:02:49.548
The candy store


00:02:50.306 --> 00:02:51.709
is a MacDonald's.


00:02:53.087 --> 00:02:54.109
And this place...


00:02:54.944 --> 00:02:57.225
a super fucking discount store.


00:02:57.434 --> 00:02:59.479
Where's the pride of ownership?


00:03:01.722 --> 00:03:03.378
Where's the personal service?


00:03:10.941 --> 00:03:12.163
See what I mean?


00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:13.656
Shit...


00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.592
What right do they have


00:03:17.871 --> 00:03:19.642
of cutting out the suppliers?


00:03:20.278 --> 00:03:22.706
Pushing out all the middlemen.


00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.106
Buying direct from the manufacturer.


00:03:28.663 --> 00:03:29.743
Sony this.


00:03:30.371 --> 00:03:31.592
Toshiba that.


00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.750
All them Chinks...


00:03:34.469 --> 00:03:36.022
put Americans out of work.


00:03:36.719 --> 00:03:39.348
<i>...plans to take place
in Quang Tri Province.</i>


00:03:39.979 --> 00:03:41.635
<i>From Laos...</i>


00:03:43.764 --> 00:03:45.396
That's the way it is now.


00:03:49.081 --> 00:03:50.437
You're all right?


00:03:51.155 --> 00:03:53.443
You can't find the heart of anything...


00:03:55.552 --> 00:03:57.020
to stick the knife.


00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:02.612
Anybody here?


00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.037
- Can I help you?
- Call an ambulance.


00:04:06.338 --> 00:04:07.552
Forget it, Frank.


00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.718
There's no one in charge.


00:04:16.931 --> 00:04:18.437
Call an ambulance!


00:04:19.779 --> 00:04:22.148
<i>Some say Bumpy Johnson
was a great man,</i>


00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.312
<i>according to eulogies,
a giving man.</i>


00:04:24.606 --> 00:04:26.710
<i>A man of the people.
No one chose to use</i>


00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.283
<i>in remembrances
the word most often associated</i>


00:04:29.403 --> 00:04:31.684
<i>with Ellsworth Bumpy Johnson:
Gangster,</i>


00:04:31.858 --> 00:04:34.183
<i>whose passing has brought
a Who's Who of mourners</i>


00:04:34.391 --> 00:04:35.636
<i>on this chilly afternoon.</i>


00:04:35.819 --> 00:04:37.870
<i>The KC mob boss,
Dominic Cattano.</i>


00:04:38.075 --> 00:04:40.208
<i>Harlem crime figure,
Nicky Barnes.</i>


00:04:40.843 --> 00:04:42.175
<i>From the political arena,</i>


00:04:42.398 --> 00:04:44.476
<i>the Governor has come down.
The Mayor of New York,</i>


00:04:44.764 --> 00:04:46.572
<i>the Chief of Police and Commissioner.</i>


00:04:46.727 --> 00:04:48.532
<i>Sports and entertainment luminaries.</i>


00:04:49.508 --> 00:04:52.132
<i>Bumpy Johnson,
age 62 when he passed</i>


00:04:52.332 --> 00:04:55.725
<i>was a folk hero among Harlem locals
for over four decades.</i>


00:04:56.264 --> 00:04:58.584
<i>Regarded by some as
the Robin Hood of Harlem,</i>


00:04:58.795 --> 00:05:01.033
<i>by others as a ruthless criminal.</i>


00:05:02.526 --> 00:05:05.040
I would've thought that Warnfield
put out a better spread.


00:05:06.854 --> 00:05:08.792
- Want some?
- No, thanks.


00:05:09.314 --> 00:05:11.028
I want chicken wings on mine.


00:05:11.813 --> 00:05:12.858
Who is that?


00:05:13.239 --> 00:05:14.903
He didn't know what hit him.


00:05:15.056 --> 00:05:16.780
I just kept poppin'
him in the face.


00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:25.429
You got a light?


00:05:38.628 --> 00:05:39.882
That's very good.


00:05:40.657 --> 00:05:41.739
Hey, Frank!


00:05:44.142 --> 00:05:45.657
Get me a light while you're at it.


00:05:48.408 --> 00:05:49.432
Appreciate it.


00:05:50.906 --> 00:05:51.952
Don Cattano.


00:05:52.386 --> 00:05:53.911
How you doing, Rossi?


00:05:55.549 --> 00:05:56.975
- Good.
- A drink, Sir?


00:05:57.174 --> 00:05:58.410
Give him a scotch.


00:06:04.881 --> 00:06:05.912
Come on.


00:06:16.436 --> 00:06:17.846
I know you're hurting, Frank.


00:06:19.106 --> 00:06:20.123
So am I.


00:06:20.866 --> 00:06:21.947
I'm all right.


00:06:22.622 --> 00:06:24.426
- You going to be all right?
- Yeah.


00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:27.459
I'm sure Bumpy didn't tell you,
but he made me promise


00:06:27.635 --> 00:06:29.455
if anything happened to him...


00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:31.071
I should make sure


00:06:31.341 --> 00:06:32.856
that you're want for nothing.


00:06:34.489 --> 00:06:35.660
I appreciate that.


00:06:36.715 --> 00:06:39.765
Half the people here
owed Bumpy money when he died.


00:06:40.464 --> 00:06:43.489
They think I'll forget to collect,
but I'll get that money.


00:06:43.971 --> 00:06:45.571
Well... that's the spirit.


00:06:46.288 --> 00:06:47.358
Go get them.


00:06:50.191 --> 00:06:51.461
<i>Mr. Roberts!</i>


00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.596
Taking the prosecution side,


00:06:53.972 --> 00:06:55.377
give us U.S. vs. Meade,


00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:58.137
subject, issues,
what the determination was


00:06:58.325 --> 00:07:00.260
and what it means to us today.


00:07:01.168 --> 00:07:02.674
Class shall be critiquing,


00:07:02.956 --> 00:07:05.020
Mr. Roberts, so pay attention.


00:07:07.811 --> 00:07:09.713
<i>I hate hearing my name,
ya know?</i>


00:07:10.181 --> 00:07:12.035
Means I gotta get up
in front of the class,


00:07:12.155 --> 00:07:15.016
I gotta turn around,
and I know everyone in there,


00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.836
they know more than I do.


00:07:17.449 --> 00:07:18.952
The N°1 fear of people...


00:07:19.161 --> 00:07:21.086
it ain't dying.
It's public speaking.


00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.947
I get physically ill.
Wanna throw up.


00:07:23.135 --> 00:07:24.777
And you wanna do that
for a living.


00:07:24.915 --> 00:07:26.910
I don't like being like that.
I want to beat it.


00:07:27.154 --> 00:07:29.303
- Should I do this?
- No, he'll take it from me.


00:07:29.456 --> 00:07:30.802
He knows me since high shool.


00:07:30.981 --> 00:07:32.684
- High school?
- Good morning.


00:07:33.023 --> 00:07:34.901
He doesn't take it, just throw it in.


00:07:35.062 --> 00:07:37.281
- That's good service.
- Throw it in?


00:07:39.129 --> 00:07:41.004
- What's up, Suzie?
- Hi, Jay.


00:07:41.124 --> 00:07:42.994
- How you doing, baby?
- All right.


00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:10.741
You, punk!


00:08:11.961 --> 00:08:14.460
You bit me, asshole!


00:08:15.764 --> 00:08:18.294
I swear to God, Richie.
I didn't know it was you.


00:08:18.888 --> 00:08:21.314
I'd never slam a door
on your hand, knowingly.


00:08:21.517 --> 00:08:22.711
You bit my fucking hand.


00:08:22.831 --> 00:08:24.534
What you doing
serving subpoenas anyway?


00:08:24.696 --> 00:08:26.585
- We're on loan to County.
- County?


00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.981
- How's that working for you?
- Fuck you.


00:08:29.547 --> 00:08:31.485
I'm sorry.
Consider me served.


00:08:31.753 --> 00:08:33.049
Can we leave it there?


00:08:33.273 --> 00:08:34.999
Assault on a police officer?


00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.426
I don't think so.


00:08:36.778 --> 00:08:39.891
For old time's sake, what can we do,
what do you want, what can I give you?


00:08:40.194 --> 00:08:42.377
What do you get for assault
with a deadly weapon, Jay?


00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:44.194
- 5 years minimum.
- 5 years.


00:08:44.619 --> 00:08:46.304
Guys, c'mon! No.


00:08:46.751 --> 00:08:48.517
Guys, what do you want?
Who do you want?


00:08:48.774 --> 00:08:50.249
- Who do you got?
- You want...


00:08:50.474 --> 00:08:52.727
Big Al's bookie, his accountant?


00:08:53.469 --> 00:08:54.911
I'll give him to you.


00:09:03.598 --> 00:09:04.938
Stop, stop.


00:09:06.153 --> 00:09:07.407
There he is.


00:09:10.254 --> 00:09:11.913
That's him. The bookie.


00:09:12.607 --> 00:09:13.834
All right. Get lost.


00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.209
- Right here?
- Right here. Get out of the car.


00:09:16.575 --> 00:09:17.722
- This is nuts.
- Come on.


00:09:18.005 --> 00:09:19.013
Let's go.


00:09:19.978 --> 00:09:20.993
Take it easy.


00:09:41.505 --> 00:09:43.095
We stay with him or the car?


00:09:43.381 --> 00:09:45.391
Let's see who comes for the car.


00:10:00.381 --> 00:10:01.763
Think he made us?


00:10:02.575 --> 00:10:05.002
You called in a warrant, right?
So where are they?


00:10:05.185 --> 00:10:06.486
I just called, man!


00:10:06.992 --> 00:10:10.302
I called and walked back here,
and ten seconds has gone by.


00:10:13.072 --> 00:10:14.853
We saw him with the slips, Jay.


00:10:15.015 --> 00:10:17.359
You saw policy slips?
You saw grocery bags.


00:10:17.603 --> 00:10:19.841
- You don't know what's in them.
- I do, and so do you.


00:10:20.004 --> 00:10:21.252
Don't give me that bull.


00:10:21.434 --> 00:10:22.735
What's the rush, Richie?


00:10:22.855 --> 00:10:25.158
- Half an hour, the warrant'll be here.
- I got night school.


00:10:25.321 --> 00:10:26.972
Guess you're gonna miss it.


00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.498
- Fuck this. Come on!
- You sure?


00:10:37.756 --> 00:10:39.189
Yeah, let's go.


00:11:32.684 --> 00:11:33.704
Fuck!


00:11:43.658 --> 00:11:44.698
Fuck!


00:12:09.107 --> 00:12:12.135
- It's not just a couple of bucks.
- It's the same thing, in principle.


00:12:13.161 --> 00:12:14.763
We're talking principles?


00:12:15.027 --> 00:12:17.161
A cop who turns in
this kind of money...


00:12:17.343 --> 00:12:20.460
says one thing.
He turns in cops who take money.


00:12:20.916 --> 00:12:23.472
- We'll be fucking pariahs.
- We're fucked both ways.


00:12:23.641 --> 00:12:26.530
Not if we keep it. Only if we don't,
then right, we're fucked,


00:12:26.672 --> 00:12:27.911
but not if we keep it.


00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:30.909
Goddamn it, man!


00:12:31.159 --> 00:12:33.291
Did we ask for it?
Did we put a gun to someone's head


00:12:33.474 --> 00:12:34.928
and say: "Give us your money"?


00:12:35.131 --> 00:12:37.366
Cops... kill cops


00:12:37.718 --> 00:12:39.078
they can't trust.


00:12:42.468 --> 00:12:43.729
We can't turn it in, man.


00:12:53.733 --> 00:12:54.860
You believe that?


00:13:04.438 --> 00:13:05.797
How much is there?


00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:09.076
Nine hundred
and eighty seven thousand.


00:13:11.088 --> 00:13:12.703
What happened to the rest?


00:13:15.895 --> 00:13:19.410
What the hell are you doing counting it
in front of everybody. Are you nuts?


00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.855
Get it back in the bags, seal'em up,
and down it to the property room.


00:13:34.913 --> 00:13:36.269
Fucking boy-scouts.


00:13:48.634 --> 00:13:50.809
So nice to see you here this evening.


00:14:00.639 --> 00:14:01.604
What?


00:14:02.657 --> 00:14:03.555
What?


00:14:27.514 --> 00:14:28.976
Detective Trupo.
Sign here.


00:14:34.017 --> 00:14:35.926
You guys ready
to make a lot of fuckin money?


00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:37.713
- Always.
- Hell yeah.


00:14:42.178 --> 00:14:43.345
Here you go!


00:14:43.969 --> 00:14:45.478
All right. Look at this.


00:14:45.785 --> 00:14:48.083
- Fucking dealers.
- Here's three more boats.


00:14:56.353 --> 00:14:58.221
Hey, don't lose any of that shit.


00:14:58.571 --> 00:15:00.317
- I know.
- Be careful.


00:15:04.743 --> 00:15:06.328
Just enough for the reagent test.


00:15:08.182 --> 00:15:09.319
A little less.


00:15:15.557 --> 00:15:17.799
<i>This is the French Connection dope.</i>


00:15:17.991 --> 00:15:21.880
<i>Kilos of the same dope Eddie Egan
and Sonny Grasso took from us!</i>


00:15:22.487 --> 00:15:24.723
<i>The cops seize it, arrest everyone,</i>


00:15:24.894 --> 00:15:27.200
<i>and they start taking it out
of the evidence room,</i>


00:15:27.396 --> 00:15:30.498
<i>whacking it down to nothing
and selling it back to us.</i>


00:15:30.954 --> 00:15:33.265
<i>They basically
control the market with it.</i>


00:15:33.468 --> 00:15:35.439
Mr. Rossi.
A surprise.


00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:38.139
<i>They've been doin this for years.
They live off it.</i>


00:15:38.338 --> 00:15:39.817
<i>- Our dope.
- Many thanks.</i>


00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.271
What the fuck is happening
to the world, Frank?


00:15:42.834 --> 00:15:44.104
Fuckin crooks.


00:15:45.535 --> 00:15:46.893
Sad about Bumpy.


00:15:49.273 --> 00:15:51.181
Things are never gonna be the same
in Harlem.


00:15:51.646 --> 00:15:53.139
You walk down the street.


00:15:53.321 --> 00:15:56.184
Nobody bothers you
cause Bumpy was making sure of it.


00:15:56.821 --> 00:15:57.918
Here, Frankie.


00:15:58.834 --> 00:16:00.257
How is it there now?


00:16:01.346 --> 00:16:03.377
It's chaos.
Every gorilla for himself.


00:16:10.638 --> 00:16:12.335
Who can live like that?


00:16:12.794 --> 00:16:14.291
There has to be order.


00:16:14.626 --> 00:16:16.453
That would've never happened
with Italians.


00:16:16.857 --> 00:16:18.985
More important than
any one man's life...


00:16:19.663 --> 00:16:20.820
is order.


00:16:28.628 --> 00:16:29.648
Frank.


00:16:32.285 --> 00:16:33.727
Come on in.
Sit down.


00:16:38.824 --> 00:16:40.164
- How y'all doin?
- Good.


00:16:40.635 --> 00:16:43.281
- So, you seen Nate over there?
- Yeah, all the time.


00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.636
Nate is everywhere.


00:16:44.852 --> 00:16:46.469
- He's good.
- He's still over there.


00:16:46.622 --> 00:16:48.105
Got himself a club now.


00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:49.740
Where, Saigon?


00:16:49.923 --> 00:16:50.959
Bangkok.


00:16:51.216 --> 00:16:52.900
I don't think he's ever comin home.


00:16:57.768 --> 00:16:58.940
Come on.


00:17:25.604 --> 00:17:28.235
On the house
for our boys in uniform.


00:17:28.533 --> 00:17:30.686
Thank you, sugar,
that's very kind.


00:17:32.044 --> 00:17:33.230
Thank Frank.


00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:34.508
Thanks, Frank.


00:17:36.336 --> 00:17:37.560
Just relax.


00:17:38.768 --> 00:17:41.184
You gonna have to boot this,
shoot a couple times.


00:17:42.703 --> 00:17:44.064
Cops keep cutting it.


00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.946
Selling the shit.


00:17:48.305 --> 00:17:50.945
I won't say anything
cause the price is right.


00:17:51.586 --> 00:17:53.087
But that shit in Nam


00:17:53.378 --> 00:17:54.674
is way...


00:17:55.679 --> 00:17:56.694
way...


00:17:57.251 --> 00:17:58.606
heavy...


00:18:23.172 --> 00:18:25.024
Didn't you see the jar, Frank?


00:18:26.353 --> 00:18:28.361
I think you walked right past it.


00:18:29.408 --> 00:18:31.200
The money jar.
What I gotta do?


00:18:31.464 --> 00:18:33.089
Put a fuckin sign on it?


00:18:37.833 --> 00:18:39.517
What are you thinking?
You know,


00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.054
Bumpy don't own 116th no more.


00:18:42.263 --> 00:18:44.903
He don't own no real estate
in Harlem right now. I'm the landlord,


00:18:45.065 --> 00:18:46.669
and the lease is 20 %.


00:18:48.521 --> 00:18:50.851
Well, don't sell dope then, Frank.


00:18:51.186 --> 00:18:53.471
Get a real job.
Need a fuckin job, Frank?


00:18:53.986 --> 00:18:56.246
Is that what you need?
You come work for me.


00:18:56.773 --> 00:18:59.402
You can drive me around.
You open my doors.


00:19:00.118 --> 00:19:03.770
Yes sir, no sir, right away sir.
Anything you want, Master Johnson.


00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:08.481
20 %.


00:19:15.915 --> 00:19:17.923
20 % is my profit, Tango.


00:19:20.633 --> 00:19:22.525
I give you that, what do I got left?
Nothing.


00:19:22.708 --> 00:19:25.719
20 % puts me and everyone you know
out of business.


00:19:26.609 --> 00:19:28.484
There are legitimate ways
of doing things,


00:19:28.768 --> 00:19:31.489
and there's this way.
Not even Bumpy took 20 %.


00:19:32.192 --> 00:19:33.613
Bumpy's fuckin dead.


00:19:37.364 --> 00:19:38.371
My man.


00:19:39.145 --> 00:19:40.165
20 %?


00:19:49.206 --> 00:19:50.326
20 %.


00:19:50.969 --> 00:19:52.416
Doc! Let's go.


00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.713
<i>The drug problem in Vietnam
is more</i>


00:19:57.922 --> 00:19:59.525
<i>than marijuana.
At this point,</i>


00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:03.416
<i>it is estimated that one third
of American troops are experimenting</i>


00:20:03.614 --> 00:20:05.299
<i>with opium and heroin.</i>


00:20:06.131 --> 00:20:07.948
<i>The authorities say they've confiscated</i>


00:20:08.131 --> 00:20:11.564
<i>large quantities of marijuana,
heroin, and pills.</i>


00:20:12.013 --> 00:20:14.619
<i>Every person and every vehicle
going through the gates</i>


00:20:14.917 --> 00:20:17.009
<i>is subject to a thorough shakedown.</i>


00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.991
<i>Soldiers have access to the drugs</i>


00:20:19.111 --> 00:20:23.308
<i>at many rest and relaxation spots
in Bangkok, Saigon, and other areas</i>


00:20:23.511 --> 00:20:25.236
<i>throughout Vietnam and Thailand.</i>


00:20:25.448 --> 00:20:27.613
<i>Officials say the easy availability</i>


00:20:27.819 --> 00:20:30.971
<i>of relatively cheap cost
of high purity heroin</i>


00:20:31.186 --> 00:20:33.217
<i>throughout Saigon and the Far East</i>


00:20:33.412 --> 00:20:35.664
<i>is leading to an epidemic
of heroin addiction</i>


00:20:35.847 --> 00:20:37.451
<i>among U.S. soldiers.</i>


00:20:41.264 --> 00:20:43.069
<i>- Operator.
- Yeah, international.</i>


00:20:43.252 --> 00:20:45.310
<i>- What city?
- Bangkok.</i>


00:20:45.493 --> 00:20:46.762
<i>You know the country code?</i>


00:20:46.905 --> 00:20:48.123
Yeah, 376.


00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:51.436
<i>- For the first 3 minutes, it'll...
- I got it, I got it.</i>


00:20:57.114 --> 00:20:58.562
<i>- Sawadeekap.
- Hello?</i>


00:20:58.682 --> 00:21:00.416
<i>"Soul brothers".
Can I help you?</i>


00:21:00.536 --> 00:21:01.497
Nate!


00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:04.008
<i>- Do I know you?
- It's me.</i>


00:21:04.251 --> 00:21:06.785
<i>- Who?
- Me, Frank! Your cousin, negro.</i>


00:21:11.097 --> 00:21:12.457
Go get yourself a new suit.


00:21:49.908 --> 00:21:51.268
Look, I'm sorry.


00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:52.702
Please, Richie.


00:21:53.214 --> 00:21:55.815
Couldn't be avoided.
I'll take him next weekend, OK?


00:21:56.923 --> 00:21:58.003
We're moving.


00:21:58.582 --> 00:22:00.205
What? Where?


00:22:02.015 --> 00:22:03.603
The St. Regis.
What do you care?


00:22:06.913 --> 00:22:08.071
My sister's.


00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:10.095
Your sister's. In Vegas?


00:22:10.523 --> 00:22:12.561
- Yeah.
- You're not moving to Las Vegas.


00:22:12.681 --> 00:22:13.970
Not with Michael.


00:22:14.553 --> 00:22:17.066
What am I supposed to do with him?
Leave him with you?


00:22:17.429 --> 00:22:18.777
There's a picture.


00:22:19.369 --> 00:22:20.881
Hey, guys!
Be cool.


00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:24.934
Laurie, Las Vegas


00:22:25.183 --> 00:22:26.970
is not the kind of place
to raise a kid.


00:22:27.235 --> 00:22:28.781
Oh, like this is a good environment?


00:22:29.209 --> 00:22:30.398
And around your friends?


00:22:30.601 --> 00:22:32.288
When am I supposed to see my boy?


00:22:32.553 --> 00:22:34.285
This weekend, last weekeend.


00:22:38.895 --> 00:22:40.561
I asked you nice to shut up, right?


00:22:40.681 --> 00:22:42.307
Now I'll have to kill you.
I swear


00:22:42.592 --> 00:22:45.052
I'll pull out my gun
and put a bullet in your fuckin head!


00:22:45.172 --> 00:22:47.113
Stop what you're doin,
and pick up the glass!


00:22:47.315 --> 00:22:48.838
Calm down, man. Be cool.


00:22:52.593 --> 00:22:53.983
He's fuckin crazy.


00:22:55.198 --> 00:22:56.396
You don't have a gun.


00:22:59.743 --> 00:23:00.819
You sure?


00:23:09.339 --> 00:23:10.856
You're crazy, Richie.


00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.967
You don't have room for us.


00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:20.714
I'll see you in court.


00:23:22.673 --> 00:23:23.809
Come on, Michael!


00:23:24.731 --> 00:23:25.963
Say bye to your dad.


00:23:27.581 --> 00:23:28.846
Hey, kiddo!


00:23:31.216 --> 00:23:33.470
See you next week.
We'll do something.


00:23:35.395 --> 00:23:37.141
Let's get you an ice cream.


00:24:02.328 --> 00:24:03.884
<i>You have 10 minutes remaining.</i>


00:24:05.143 --> 00:24:06.316
10 minutes.


00:25:20.073 --> 00:25:22.814
Girl, don't talk.
I wanna do a little funk.


00:26:00.787 --> 00:26:01.889
How much you want?


00:26:03.625 --> 00:26:05.362
Tell him I want a 100 kis.


00:26:07.910 --> 00:26:09.879
Ain't nobody I know
who can get you that much.


00:26:10.042 --> 00:26:12.133
You have to piece it together
from different sources.


00:26:12.377 --> 00:26:14.001
And it's not gonna be 100 % pure.


00:26:14.895 --> 00:26:16.218
I don't want that.


00:26:16.486 --> 00:26:18.054
I know what you don't want.


00:26:18.225 --> 00:26:22.478
But you'll need to get
to the Chi-Chou syndicate, all right?


00:26:23.078 --> 00:26:25.480
In Cholon, Saigon.
If they'll deal with you at all.


00:26:25.643 --> 00:26:28.063
I understand, but
by then, it'll be too late.


00:26:28.215 --> 00:26:30.785
It'll be already chopped up.
I want to get it where they get it from.


00:26:30.905 --> 00:26:31.944
The source.


00:26:32.208 --> 00:26:34.279
- And get it yourself?
- Why not?


00:26:36.352 --> 00:26:37.553
I came this far.


00:26:38.206 --> 00:26:40.866
- You'd go into the motherfuckin jungle?
- I'm in it. Look around,


00:26:41.058 --> 00:26:42.998
They're eating these roaches,
whatever that is.


00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:44.663
Nigga, I'm talking about snakes.


00:26:44.985 --> 00:26:49.371
Tigers, Vietcongs, mosquitos
that'll fuckin kill your ass.


00:26:51.681 --> 00:26:53.593
- You wanna go into the jungle?
- We're going.


00:26:56.508 --> 00:26:58.043
- Fuck it, let's go.
- We're going.


00:26:58.186 --> 00:26:59.180
Why not?


00:27:42.194 --> 00:27:43.267
Hey, Frank.


00:27:44.495 --> 00:27:47.404
This whole spot's locked down
by the Kuomintang.


00:27:49.126 --> 00:27:51.403
General Chang Kai Chek's
defeated army.


00:28:30.282 --> 00:28:32.221
How would you get it into the States?


00:28:32.705 --> 00:28:34.483
You ain't got to worry about that.


00:28:34.654 --> 00:28:37.903
- Who do you work for in there?
- Don't worry about that either.


00:28:38.527 --> 00:28:39.667
Who are you really?


00:28:40.835 --> 00:28:42.897
Frank Lucas,
like it says on my passport.


00:28:43.115 --> 00:28:45.634
- I mean, who you represent?
- Me.


00:28:48.237 --> 00:28:51.904
You think you're going to take
a 100 kilos of heroin into the U.S.


00:28:52.064 --> 00:28:55.332
and you don't work for anyone?
Someone's going to allow that?


00:28:56.306 --> 00:28:57.410
That's right.


00:29:04.760 --> 00:29:06.710
After this first purchase...


00:29:07.388 --> 00:29:10.018
if you're not killed
by Marseilles importers...


00:29:10.723 --> 00:29:12.918
or their people in the States...


00:29:13.786 --> 00:29:15.626
then, what?


00:29:16.312 --> 00:29:19.159
Then there'll be more, much more.
I guarantee you.


00:29:19.963 --> 00:29:23.111
And if it's all the same to you, I don't
have to drag my ass here no more.


00:29:24.842 --> 00:29:25.956
Of course not.


00:29:29.161 --> 00:29:30.185
My man.


00:29:31.161 --> 00:29:33.277
- Soul brothers?
- Soul brothers.


00:30:15.461 --> 00:30:19.539
Fifty grand. It'll cover them,
the pilot and the boys on the other end.


00:30:20.796 --> 00:30:22.223
Give them a hundred.


00:30:23.246 --> 00:30:24.680
Fifty will cover it.


00:30:25.294 --> 00:30:27.466
Give them a hundred, the whole thing.


00:30:28.263 --> 00:30:29.283
And look.


00:30:30.324 --> 00:30:31.550
That's all I got.


00:30:31.703 --> 00:30:34.242
If that dope don't arrive,
for any reason...


00:30:38.001 --> 00:30:39.021
Listen.


00:30:39.479 --> 00:30:42.050
Cousin or no cousin,
I'm a busy man, all right?


00:30:42.261 --> 00:30:44.616
I got no time to go
to nobody's funeral.


00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:47.993
I'll let you know
when it's in the air.


00:30:48.620 --> 00:30:49.635
My man.


00:31:13.599 --> 00:31:15.921
<i>Richie?
Fuckin guy made me,</i>


00:31:16.224 --> 00:31:18.052
don't know how he did,
but he did.


00:31:18.659 --> 00:31:19.959
<i>He went for his gun!</i>


00:31:20.250 --> 00:31:21.625
I had to do it, man!


00:31:21.782 --> 00:31:23.233
A hundred people out there heard


00:31:23.446 --> 00:31:25.549
the shot. You gotta help me,
you gotta do something!


00:31:27.836 --> 00:31:28.999
Where are you, Jay?


00:31:30.312 --> 00:31:31.674
That's the problem.


00:31:35.013 --> 00:31:36.733
Dispatch, I got a 10-13.


00:31:36.913 --> 00:31:38.247
I got a 10-13.


00:31:38.722 --> 00:31:40.445
<i>Copy that. What's your 20?</i>


00:31:41.228 --> 00:31:42.388
Tower 2.


00:31:44.329 --> 00:31:45.532
Floor 1G.


00:31:46.593 --> 00:31:48.482
Canton West, in the projects.


00:31:48.766 --> 00:31:51.472
<i>- Identify yourself, please.
- Detective Richard Roberts.</i>


00:31:51.816 --> 00:31:54.158
<i>Negative, I got no units in that area.</i>


00:31:54.422 --> 00:31:55.437
Bullshit.


00:31:56.111 --> 00:31:58.526
Please put the call out again.
I'll need assistance.


00:31:58.759 --> 00:32:02.130
<i>Det. Roberts, I got no units
in that area, that's a negative.</i>


00:32:29.798 --> 00:32:31.684
Why you goin' thru, motherfucker?


00:32:33.307 --> 00:32:34.430
Be cool!


00:32:34.609 --> 00:32:36.079
Be cool, all right?


00:32:36.298 --> 00:32:38.379
I'll find out what's going on in here.


00:32:47.431 --> 00:32:48.479
Richie.


00:32:55.280 --> 00:32:57.037
<i>Open the motherfuckin door!</i>


00:32:57.189 --> 00:32:58.468
Where's your backup?


00:33:00.031 --> 00:33:01.879
You got no backup?
Why is that?


00:33:05.906 --> 00:33:06.921
Bandage his neck.


00:33:07.083 --> 00:33:09.701
- Richie, he's dead.
- I know he's fuckin dead, right?


00:33:09.899 --> 00:33:12.527
Bandage his neck, clean up his head.
Prop him up on the gurney


00:33:12.689 --> 00:33:14.663
so he's sittin,
and open his fuckin eyes.


00:33:15.220 --> 00:33:17.343
- All right? Let's go!
- Fuck.


00:33:21.655 --> 00:33:23.057
OK, clean him up.


00:33:34.610 --> 00:33:35.666
Give me your gun.


00:33:35.937 --> 00:33:36.993
Your gun!


00:33:40.305 --> 00:33:41.425
You have your badge?


00:33:44.350 --> 00:33:45.460
You guys ready?


00:33:45.809 --> 00:33:47.434
Just keep moving forward.


00:33:48.542 --> 00:33:49.780
- You all right?
- Yeah.


00:33:51.850 --> 00:33:53.393
It's OK!


00:33:53.962 --> 00:33:55.600
Injured man coming out.
Step back.


00:33:59.018 --> 00:34:00.845
Let them do their job.
He'll be all right.


00:34:03.417 --> 00:34:04.453
Step back.


00:34:07.316 --> 00:34:08.926
That's fine.
That's it.


00:34:11.436 --> 00:34:12.655
He's alive.


00:34:13.879 --> 00:34:15.258
What happened inside?


00:34:26.121 --> 00:34:27.183
Thanks, man.


00:34:28.639 --> 00:34:29.651
Fuck.


00:34:30.561 --> 00:34:33.160
The asshole pulled a piece on me.
Can you fuckin believe it?


00:34:33.352 --> 00:34:35.916
He pulls a piece on a cop?
Had to do it, man.


00:34:36.119 --> 00:34:37.439
Kill or be killed.


00:34:38.438 --> 00:34:40.118
Fuckin crazy world, right?


00:34:43.318 --> 00:34:45.189
What the fuck were you doing
on the projects?


00:34:45.432 --> 00:34:47.886
Investigating stuff, man,
you know.


00:34:48.886 --> 00:34:50.327
Just like you taught me.


00:34:50.710 --> 00:34:53.289
Checking on guys,
following things up,


00:34:53.450 --> 00:34:55.135
putting the pieces together.


00:34:55.844 --> 00:34:58.565
The guy was a fucking dealer.
Scum of the earth!


00:35:00.472 --> 00:35:02.874
That guy
didn't pull a gun on a cop, Jay.


00:35:03.479 --> 00:35:05.043
That guy pulled a gun on a junkie.


00:35:06.153 --> 00:35:07.630
The junkie was trying to rob him.


00:35:07.840 --> 00:35:09.282
What the fuck you sayin?


00:35:10.872 --> 00:35:12.821
What the fuck you doin, man?


00:35:13.025 --> 00:35:15.231
- What the fuck is that?
- That money's mine, man!


00:35:15.479 --> 00:35:17.164
I earned this shit!
It's mine!


00:35:17.405 --> 00:35:19.050
I earned it doing good cop work.


00:35:19.371 --> 00:35:21.760
- I got it doin good cop work!
- You murdered him!


00:35:21.943 --> 00:35:24.054
- And gettin shot at!
- You murdered the guy!


00:35:24.971 --> 00:35:26.791
You murdered him,
you robbed his money,


00:35:26.990 --> 00:35:28.483
then you called me to get you out.


00:35:28.608 --> 00:35:30.222
Makes me an accessory after the fact.


00:35:30.416 --> 00:35:31.603
I'll tell you the facts,


00:35:31.761 --> 00:35:34.264
just write the report
the way i see it happened.


00:35:34.495 --> 00:35:36.248
And then that's the way it is.


00:35:36.483 --> 00:35:38.351
And that's how it'll all be.


00:35:39.542 --> 00:35:40.709
I can't do that.


00:35:42.018 --> 00:35:45.604
I'm a leper because I listened to you
and turned in a million bucks.


00:35:45.956 --> 00:35:47.715
No one will work with me after that.


00:35:48.666 --> 00:35:51.041
I can give up this shit, Richie!


00:35:51.583 --> 00:35:52.679
That's easy.


00:35:53.302 --> 00:35:54.836
Just write the report.


00:35:55.358 --> 00:35:56.461
Between us.


00:35:56.821 --> 00:35:57.879
As partners.


00:35:59.610 --> 00:36:00.841
I can't do that.


00:36:07.054 --> 00:36:08.043
Stop!


00:36:47.907 --> 00:36:49.064
Open the trunk.


00:37:11.975 --> 00:37:14.716
<i>Get out!
Get out of Vietnam!</i>


00:37:18.108 --> 00:37:21.222
<i>As loud as we can
that the Vietnam war should stop,</i>


00:37:21.405 --> 00:37:24.477
<i>and that the best way to stop it
is for the United States</i>


00:37:24.712 --> 00:37:27.988
<i>to simply pack up
and get out of Vietnam right now!</i>


00:37:33.542 --> 00:37:34.943
How are we looking?


00:37:37.938 --> 00:37:41.286
Typically what I see
is 25 to 45 % pure.


00:37:41.641 --> 00:37:44.507
There are no adulterants, no alkaloids,
no dilutents.


00:37:45.623 --> 00:37:47.134
It's a hundred percent.


00:37:52.445 --> 00:37:54.308
- May I?
- Take it with you.


00:37:56.076 --> 00:37:57.132
Thank you, Frank.


00:39:53.904 --> 00:39:54.953
I'll take it.


00:39:55.136 --> 00:39:57.528
No contingencies, no loan,
no nothing.


00:39:59.023 --> 00:40:00.038
Cash.


00:40:01.260 --> 00:40:02.353
Fabulous.


00:40:07.390 --> 00:40:09.589
I’m not talking
about your proclivities.


00:40:09.815 --> 00:40:12.954
Those I only know too well.
I’m talking about being a cop.


00:40:13.943 --> 00:40:15.830
You talking about taking money?


00:40:16.466 --> 00:40:17.867
I don't do that.
Not my thing.


00:40:18.118 --> 00:40:20.537
And your friends from the hood,
still hang out with them?


00:40:21.219 --> 00:40:22.863
Yeah. Play baseball on the weekends.


00:40:23.265 --> 00:40:25.316
Wise guys?
It's gonna look good.


00:40:26.146 --> 00:40:28.252
Guys I went to school with, so what?


00:40:28.548 --> 00:40:30.175
What about Joseph Sadano?


00:40:31.896 --> 00:40:32.981
What about him?


00:40:33.192 --> 00:40:35.757
I’m just trying to understand
things your wife has said.


00:40:35.938 --> 00:40:38.655
- If they're not true, tell me.
- Yeah, he’s one of them.


00:40:39.121 --> 00:40:41.125
Is he also your son’s godfather?


00:40:41.748 --> 00:40:43.292
He's definitely fucking her.


00:40:43.586 --> 00:40:45.255
Do you really care about this?


00:40:45.867 --> 00:40:48.213
Or do you just not want her
to win ever?


00:40:52.004 --> 00:40:55.219
You know there's an interview room?
On the second floor.


00:40:55.470 --> 00:40:57.663
- That's what I thought.
- Door locks from the inside.


00:40:57.939 --> 00:40:59.062
All rise!


00:41:07.267 --> 00:41:09.094
Fuck me like a cop, not a lawyer.


00:41:19.090 --> 00:41:20.161
Don't answer!


00:41:41.801 --> 00:41:43.573
- Richie Roberts.
- Hey, Norm!


00:41:46.541 --> 00:41:48.649
- Richie Roberts.
- Hi, Det. Norman Riley.


00:41:48.811 --> 00:41:50.476
- Hi, Norman. How are you?
- Good.


00:41:51.786 --> 00:41:53.147
- Is that him?
- Yeah.


00:42:01.667 --> 00:42:04.484
Nice night to come out, huh?
It's like Grand Central around here.


00:42:05.321 --> 00:42:06.626
It's been like this.


00:42:07.084 --> 00:42:08.810
I'm lucky if I get home by midnight.


00:42:09.450 --> 00:42:11.022
It's like nothing we've seen before.


00:42:16.405 --> 00:42:17.770
Something I gotta sign?


00:42:18.149 --> 00:42:19.612
Yeah, this way.


00:42:20.398 --> 00:42:22.921
I'm taking this with me.
I'll register it, all right?


00:42:26.696 --> 00:42:29.095
<i>America's public enemy number one</i>


00:42:29.324 --> 00:42:32.042
<i>in the United States
is drug abuse.</i>


00:42:33.620 --> 00:42:35.518
<i>In order
to fight and defeat this ennemy,</i>


00:42:35.710 --> 00:42:37.424
<i>It is necessary to wage</i>


00:42:38.072 --> 00:42:39.635
<i>a new all out offensive.</i>


00:42:41.091 --> 00:42:43.595
<i>Federal authorities
have announced their intention</i>


00:42:43.736 --> 00:42:47.045
<i>to establish special
narcotics bureaus in Washington</i>


00:42:47.204 --> 00:42:49.037
<i>New York, Los Angeles, Chicago...</i>


00:42:49.228 --> 00:42:50.975
A detective without the support


00:42:51.198 --> 00:42:53.480
of his fellow detectives
really can't do much.


00:42:55.507 --> 00:42:57.010
You know why I don't have it.


00:42:58.353 --> 00:43:00.509
Doesn't matter.
You do what you have to do.


00:43:01.449 --> 00:43:04.455
The greatest city in the world
is turning into an open sewer.


00:43:05.580 --> 00:43:07.018
Everybody's stealing.


00:43:07.990 --> 00:43:09.036
Dealing.


00:43:10.313 --> 00:43:12.362
You can't work
because you did your job!


00:43:13.822 --> 00:43:16.624
Good news is you're not
the only honest cop in town.


00:43:17.236 --> 00:43:19.183
This special narcotics bureau
in Washington


00:43:19.345 --> 00:43:21.150
is not a dog and pony show.


00:43:21.998 --> 00:43:23.200
They're sincere.


00:43:23.367 --> 00:43:25.376
I know it because
they want us to orchestrate it


00:43:25.537 --> 00:43:27.829
and I want you
to head up things here on our end.


00:43:28.104 --> 00:43:29.667
If it's federal,
who do I answer to?


00:43:29.830 --> 00:43:31.366
- Post office?
- You answer to me.


00:43:31.617 --> 00:43:33.911
Me and the U.S. Attorney,
nobody else.


00:43:36.037 --> 00:43:38.162
You never step foot
in a police station again,


00:43:38.561 --> 00:43:39.927
work out at your own place.


00:43:40.122 --> 00:43:41.384
You pick your own guys,


00:43:41.533 --> 00:43:44.870
Guys that you know wouldn’t
take a nickel off the sidewalk.


00:44:07.308 --> 00:44:08.762
<i>- Huey.
- Huey!</i>


00:44:09.227 --> 00:44:10.713
<i>- What of what?
- Who's this?</i>


00:44:10.998 --> 00:44:12.054
Who you think, boy?


00:44:12.776 --> 00:44:14.360
<i>- Frank!
- Frank who?</i>


00:44:14.813 --> 00:44:16.234
<i>Your brother, negro.</i>


00:44:20.403 --> 00:44:22.079
- That's right.
- Marvin!


00:44:22.561 --> 00:44:23.759
- Where's Ma?
- What?


00:44:24.145 --> 00:44:25.931
Where's...
Frank's on the phone!


00:44:26.347 --> 00:44:27.626
How you doin, Frankie?


00:44:27.778 --> 00:44:29.223
Frank, on the phone!


00:44:30.251 --> 00:44:32.465
- Say what?
- Ma, Frank on the phone!


00:44:32.906 --> 00:44:33.929
Oh, my Lord!


00:44:34.156 --> 00:44:36.267
Yo, when?
You just say it, man.


00:44:36.441 --> 00:44:37.627
<i>I'll call you back</i>


00:44:37.821 --> 00:44:40.196
at 6 o'clock.
Get everybody together, all right?


00:44:40.371 --> 00:44:41.386
Mama, everybody.


00:45:02.888 --> 00:45:04.347
How you doin, Uncle Frank?


00:45:05.143 --> 00:45:06.949
Get out of the car!
It's here.


00:45:08.521 --> 00:45:09.586
Look at this!


00:45:10.479 --> 00:45:11.737
My Lord!


00:45:12.102 --> 00:45:14.008
So glad to see you, boy.


00:45:14.714 --> 00:45:18.913
I'm telling you,
some piece of land you got here.


00:45:20.398 --> 00:45:22.855
- I wonder what the Boro people'd say.
- And whose house is that?


00:45:23.153 --> 00:45:24.891
That is your house, Mama.


00:45:25.719 --> 00:45:27.302
- Mine?
- That's yours.


00:45:28.914 --> 00:45:30.093
And who else?


00:45:45.161 --> 00:45:46.164
Listen!


00:45:46.344 --> 00:45:48.334
I wanna tell you how happy I am.


00:45:48.659 --> 00:45:50.660
Seeing all my children at the table,


00:45:50.843 --> 00:45:52.992
and the grand children
at the same time.


00:45:53.424 --> 00:45:54.621
I'm so happy!


00:45:54.967 --> 00:45:56.997
- Right on, Grandma!
- Enjoy yourselves.


00:45:57.393 --> 00:45:59.395
I hope you got a job,
the way you eatin all this.


00:45:59.864 --> 00:46:01.884
That boy, he got an arm on him.


00:46:02.657 --> 00:46:03.738
A Major League arm.


00:46:03.950 --> 00:46:05.270
- Oh yeah?
- Right?


00:46:06.326 --> 00:46:07.341
Right on, Pop.


00:46:07.624 --> 00:46:10.261
After dinner,
let's see him throw around a bit.


00:46:10.610 --> 00:46:11.991
You can't catch him, man.


00:46:12.162 --> 00:46:14.875
I'm telling you,
he throws harder than Gibson.


00:46:15.559 --> 00:46:17.580
We're talking 95 miles an hour.


00:46:17.867 --> 00:46:18.903
Can you catch him?


00:46:20.192 --> 00:46:21.625
He'd go catch the grass.


00:46:21.810 --> 00:46:24.479
He might have catched that thing
when I was about 5 years old.


00:46:24.783 --> 00:46:26.266
Since then, he can't keep up.


00:46:30.044 --> 00:46:31.633
This is your room.


00:46:31.788 --> 00:46:32.824
Perfect.


00:46:35.812 --> 00:46:37.083
Look at this.


00:46:40.104 --> 00:46:41.351
It's beautiful.


00:46:41.597 --> 00:46:43.216
Real beautiful, this.


00:46:51.541 --> 00:46:52.681
How did you...


00:46:53.083 --> 00:46:54.263
I had it made.


00:46:56.220 --> 00:46:57.367
From memory.


00:46:57.622 --> 00:46:59.235
You were 5 when they took it away.


00:46:59.417 --> 00:47:00.760
- Right.
- How could you...


00:47:00.943 --> 00:47:02.527
How could I forget, Mamma?


00:47:07.388 --> 00:47:08.954
I thought you did.


00:47:09.776 --> 00:47:11.295
It, it... is perfect.


00:47:11.755 --> 00:47:13.398
It's all perfect.


00:47:18.956 --> 00:47:21.380
I can't tell you
how much I love you.


00:47:21.771 --> 00:47:23.174
I love you too, Mother.


00:47:24.545 --> 00:47:25.548
It's okay.


00:47:34.083 --> 00:47:37.606
Both these guys, good with wires.
They got solid informants.


00:47:37.985 --> 00:47:39.293
They're honest.


00:47:39.466 --> 00:47:40.682
And fearless.


00:47:41.023 --> 00:47:42.958
They're insane, Richie,
like you.


00:47:43.941 --> 00:47:45.048
Where are they?


00:47:48.506 --> 00:47:50.653
That's Jones,
with the skinny white broad.


00:47:51.262 --> 00:47:53.018
Best I've ever seen on the street.


00:47:53.180 --> 00:47:55.739
He knows dope,
but he's together.


00:47:57.042 --> 00:47:58.727
He's a stand up guy, all around.


00:47:59.375 --> 00:48:00.677
That's Abruzzo


00:48:00.941 --> 00:48:02.589
with the two black fat ones.


00:48:03.210 --> 00:48:05.501
He loves a big ass, man.


00:48:07.341 --> 00:48:08.686
He's a bulldog.


00:48:09.243 --> 00:48:11.889
He don't fuck around,
he got a bit of a temper yeah, but,


00:48:12.149 --> 00:48:14.403
you could trust this guy
with your grandma.


00:48:14.908 --> 00:48:15.917
Listen.


00:48:16.246 --> 00:48:19.170
We work together. You want me,
you got to take them, too.


00:48:31.824 --> 00:48:32.961
When do we start?


00:48:36.072 --> 00:48:37.328
<i>The man I worked for</i>


00:48:37.486 --> 00:48:41.268
ran one of the biggest companies
in New York City for more than 50 years.


00:48:41.965 --> 00:48:43.290
15 years,


00:48:43.595 --> 00:48:45.337
8 months and 9 days


00:48:45.843 --> 00:48:47.153
I was with him every day,


00:48:47.460 --> 00:48:50.029
protected him, looked after him.
I learned from him.


00:48:51.907 --> 00:48:54.169
Bumpy was rich,
but wasn't white man rich.


00:48:54.372 --> 00:48:55.648
He wasn't wealthy.


00:48:56.219 --> 00:48:58.298
He didn’t own his own company.
He thought he did.


00:48:58.490 --> 00:48:59.693
He just managed it.


00:49:00.174 --> 00:49:01.926
White men owned it,
so they owned him.


00:49:02.754 --> 00:49:04.060
Nobody owns me though.


00:49:04.319 --> 00:49:05.830
- How you doin, babe?
- Good.


00:49:06.272 --> 00:49:09.057
Cause I own my own company,
and my company sells a product


00:49:09.254 --> 00:49:11.203
that’s better than the competition’s.


00:49:12.261 --> 00:49:14.714
At a price that’s lower
than the competition’s.


00:49:16.102 --> 00:49:17.442
What are we selling here?


00:49:33.383 --> 00:49:34.527
How you doin, Red?


00:49:35.423 --> 00:49:37.332
My brothers,
just got here from North Carolina,


00:49:37.535 --> 00:49:38.753
Guys, this is Redtop.


00:49:39.672 --> 00:49:41.174
- How you doin?
- And the ladies.


00:49:41.337 --> 00:49:42.487
Nice family.


00:49:42.721 --> 00:49:44.949
What? Ya'll niggas
never seen hoochie before?


00:49:45.875 --> 00:49:46.991
Why they all naked?


00:49:47.251 --> 00:49:48.712
So they can steal nothin.


00:49:51.592 --> 00:49:54.106
Most important thing in business
is honesty.


00:49:54.582 --> 00:49:56.045
Integrity, hard work.


00:49:57.447 --> 00:49:58.454
Family.


00:49:59.583 --> 00:50:01.377
Never forgetting
where we came from.


00:50:01.884 --> 00:50:03.092
Thank you, Charlene.


00:50:08.525 --> 00:50:10.708
See, you are what you are
in this world.


00:50:11.775 --> 00:50:13.591
That's either one of two things.


00:50:15.266 --> 00:50:16.799
Either you're somebody.


00:50:18.206 --> 00:50:20.137
Or nobody.
I'll be right back.


00:50:36.497 --> 00:50:37.603
I need this fresh,


00:50:37.840 --> 00:50:39.913
cause if I come back here,
you'll know what it is.


00:50:40.123 --> 00:50:41.687
- You don't play that.
- I hear you,


00:50:41.870 --> 00:50:44.459
you won't have to come back.
There will be no problem.


00:50:45.523 --> 00:50:46.571
Where's my money?


00:50:46.774 --> 00:50:49.259
Redtop gave you the package,
you supposed to hand me my money.


00:50:49.462 --> 00:50:51.205
Here's a jar right here.
20 %.


00:50:51.461 --> 00:50:53.126
- You got the jar?
- That's right.


00:50:54.700 --> 00:50:55.960
Get the fuck outa here...


00:50:56.223 --> 00:50:58.337
What you gonna do?
What the fuck you gonna do?


00:50:59.651 --> 00:51:00.666
What you doin?


00:51:00.889 --> 00:51:02.818
You wanna shoot me,
in front of everybody?


00:51:03.050 --> 00:51:04.106
Huh? Come on!


00:51:06.886 --> 00:51:07.927
Shit.


00:51:20.137 --> 00:51:21.176
Here you go.


00:51:21.822 --> 00:51:22.843
20 %.


00:51:46.593 --> 00:51:48.083
So, what was I sayin?


00:51:58.817 --> 00:52:02.083
This is the newly formed
Essex County narcotics squad.


00:52:03.551 --> 00:52:07.337
Our mandate is to make major arrests.
No street guys.


00:52:08.276 --> 00:52:10.911
We're looking for the suppliers
and the distributors.


00:52:11.431 --> 00:52:13.092
Heroin, cocaine, amphetamines.


00:52:13.256 --> 00:52:15.997
No grass under 1,000 pounds.
No powder under 40 kilos.


00:52:16.373 --> 00:52:18.395
Less than that,
someone else can waste their time.


00:52:18.598 --> 00:52:20.696
We'll be handling big shipments,
big money,


00:52:20.923 --> 00:52:22.140
and big temptation.


00:52:22.311 --> 00:52:24.286
I heard a story about you.
That you found


00:52:24.565 --> 00:52:27.595
a million $ in unmarked cash.
And you gave that shit back.


00:52:28.083 --> 00:52:29.119
Is that true?


00:52:29.950 --> 00:52:31.792
Yeah, I did.
Anyone got a problem with that?


00:52:37.186 --> 00:52:39.153
So do I.
I think about it everyday.


00:52:39.347 --> 00:52:42.362
I should be down in Florida with
a 68 full cruiser dual, fishing sharks.


00:52:42.507 --> 00:52:44.096
- You and me both.
- But you know...


00:52:44.279 --> 00:52:46.266
I didn't, so here I am, and...


00:52:47.782 --> 00:52:49.636
We'll try to land
some other kinda sharks.


00:53:16.952 --> 00:53:18.368
- All right?
- Bingo.


00:53:42.233 --> 00:53:43.233
See that?


00:53:44.598 --> 00:53:46.486
And this stuff is everyday's stuff.


00:53:47.353 --> 00:53:48.748
But this Blue Magic,


00:53:48.931 --> 00:53:50.291
twice the potency.


00:53:50.608 --> 00:53:52.853
The purest thing
I've ever seen in the street.


00:53:53.233 --> 00:53:54.789
Strong enough to smoke.


00:53:55.402 --> 00:53:58.013
That's for those suburban
white kids scared of needles.


00:53:58.426 --> 00:54:00.009
You paid 10 bucks for that?


00:54:00.277 --> 00:54:02.708
And it's everywhere,
on every corner.


00:54:02.926 --> 00:54:04.495
So how's that possible?


00:54:04.979 --> 00:54:08.163
Who can afford to sell shit
twice as good for half as much?


00:54:16.535 --> 00:54:19.084
Hey man, good to see you!


00:54:19.421 --> 00:54:21.127
- Doin good?
- Yeah, just got back


00:54:21.333 --> 00:54:22.933
from a trip to the south of France.


00:54:38.050 --> 00:54:39.458
Know what I'm sayin?


00:54:40.948 --> 00:54:42.166
Here you go!


00:54:46.974 --> 00:54:48.193
Who is that?


00:54:59.632 --> 00:55:01.139
Ladies and gentlemen.


00:55:01.540 --> 00:55:03.765
The Proud Bomber, the champ.


00:55:04.333 --> 00:55:05.947
Mr. Joe Louis!


00:55:15.093 --> 00:55:16.448
Who's that with Joe?


00:55:16.908 --> 00:55:18.177
Miss Puerto Rico.


00:55:19.006 --> 00:55:20.064
Puerto Rico?


00:55:20.839 --> 00:55:23.519
- She a beauty queen.
- Real. The beauty queen.


00:55:49.969 --> 00:55:51.350
My main man.


00:55:56.570 --> 00:55:58.283
Excuse us for a minute, please.


00:55:58.439 --> 00:55:59.616
Sure, Frank.


00:56:02.109 --> 00:56:03.109
Thank you.


00:56:07.497 --> 00:56:08.526
What's goin on?


00:56:08.737 --> 00:56:09.970
What you smiling about?


00:56:10.136 --> 00:56:11.517
- I dunno.
- What is this?


00:56:11.886 --> 00:56:12.982
What's what?


00:56:13.366 --> 00:56:14.684
- What?
- Come here.


00:56:17.013 --> 00:56:18.215
What's that you wearin?


00:56:18.457 --> 00:56:19.613
What's what?


00:56:20.416 --> 00:56:21.951
That, what you got on?


00:56:22.180 --> 00:56:23.805
A very, very, very nice suit.


00:56:23.986 --> 00:56:25.376
Very, very nice suit, huh?


00:56:25.557 --> 00:56:27.259
That's a clown suit,
a costume, man,


00:56:27.517 --> 00:56:29.608
with a big sign that says:
"Arrest me".


00:56:29.882 --> 00:56:32.357
Understand? You too loud,
you're making too much noise.


00:56:32.547 --> 00:56:34.638
Look at me.
The loudest one in the room


00:56:35.123 --> 00:56:37.763
is the weakest one in the room,
I tell you that.


00:56:38.555 --> 00:56:41.448
- You tryin to be like Nicky Barnes?
- What's the problem with him?


00:56:41.655 --> 00:56:43.799
- I like him.
- I got no problem. You like him?


00:56:44.153 --> 00:56:46.081
You wanna be like him?
You wanna be Superfly?


00:56:46.401 --> 00:56:47.795
You wanna work for him?


00:56:47.983 --> 00:56:49.709
Share a jail cell with him?
Cook for him?


00:56:49.871 --> 00:56:52.985
- He wants to talk to you.
- So, you talkin to him about me now?


00:56:53.200 --> 00:56:54.513
What about?


00:56:54.649 --> 00:56:56.326
- It ain't like that.
- Then what is it?


00:56:56.471 --> 00:56:58.381
- Your name came up.
- About what?


00:56:58.998 --> 00:57:01.280
I don't know, I told him I'd tell you.


00:57:03.688 --> 00:57:04.978
You know, boy...


00:57:07.183 --> 00:57:09.562
If you wasn't my bro', I'd kill you.
You know that?


00:57:09.714 --> 00:57:11.727
I'd blow your fuckin brains out.


00:57:11.893 --> 00:57:14.208
- Don't be like that.
- I'm taking you shoppin this week.


00:57:14.353 --> 00:57:15.897
- I can do it alone.
- I can tell.


00:57:49.984 --> 00:57:51.368
You still owe me that dance.


00:57:51.667 --> 00:57:52.667
Doc, come on.


00:57:53.100 --> 00:57:54.149
Frank.


00:57:54.718 --> 00:57:55.733
Check this.


00:58:06.263 --> 00:58:07.705
- How you doing?
- Hi.


00:58:08.027 --> 00:58:09.979
- Frank Lucas.
- Eva Jendo.


00:58:10.820 --> 00:58:11.978
Nice to meet you, Eva.


00:58:12.262 --> 00:58:13.805
Nice to meet you, Frank.


00:58:15.055 --> 00:58:16.872
You're Frank,
and this is your place.


00:58:17.206 --> 00:58:19.613
That's right, I'm Frank
and this is my place.


00:58:25.817 --> 00:58:27.462
Why is it called Small's?


00:58:27.807 --> 00:58:29.235
Why not Frank's?


00:58:31.025 --> 00:58:33.211
When you own something,
you call it what you want.


00:58:34.623 --> 00:58:35.682
Small's.


00:58:36.203 --> 00:58:37.360
Or Frank's.


00:58:37.882 --> 00:58:39.007
Frankie Small's.


00:58:39.344 --> 00:58:40.380
Small's Frankie.


00:58:42.325 --> 00:58:43.363
That's right.


00:58:44.411 --> 00:58:45.816
You want to let my hand go?


00:58:48.010 --> 00:58:49.010
Okay.


00:58:50.404 --> 00:58:51.509
You're leaving?


00:58:51.793 --> 00:58:53.296
No, I was going to my table.


00:58:53.580 --> 00:58:55.306
You need someone to go with you?


00:58:57.939 --> 00:58:58.995
Yes?


00:59:05.476 --> 00:59:07.225
Wash your hand?
I got one print of that.


00:59:07.398 --> 00:59:08.576
You'll smudge it.


00:59:10.543 --> 00:59:12.573
- Here you go.
- What about him?


00:59:12.754 --> 00:59:14.231
- Who's that?
- Joey Sadano.


00:59:14.383 --> 00:59:15.729
Don Cattano's nephew.


00:59:16.193 --> 00:59:18.813
- Put him up there by the big man
- He looks like you, Abruzzo.


00:59:18.959 --> 00:59:20.010
Not as handsome.


00:59:20.200 --> 00:59:22.468
- Looks more like your sister.
- Where's Ice Pick Paul?


00:59:22.640 --> 00:59:24.762
Funny. You guys should
take that show on the road.


00:59:25.097 --> 00:59:26.769
So we need...
Ice Pick Paul.


00:59:28.771 --> 00:59:29.831
There you go.


00:59:31.278 --> 00:59:32.696
He goes near the top.


00:59:33.258 --> 00:59:36.246
No, Ice Pick Paul is a soldier,
this guy is a lieutenant.


00:59:36.510 --> 00:59:38.597
"... you have passed the
New Jersey Bar Examination. "


00:59:40.584 --> 00:59:42.056
That guy is a soldier.


00:59:42.218 --> 00:59:44.170
This guy's a lieutenant.
No way he's on top.


00:59:44.332 --> 00:59:46.647
You're thinking Benny the Bishop.
Benny Two Socks,


00:59:46.783 --> 00:59:49.785
- Cattano's deadbeat son-in-law.
- Jonesy's right.


00:59:50.098 --> 00:59:53.152
Which one of you has actually seen
Ice Pick Paul selling drugs?


00:59:53.796 --> 00:59:54.813
Actually,


00:59:55.057 --> 00:59:56.950
- seen it go down?
- Yeah, seen it go down,


00:59:57.098 --> 00:59:59.202
been in his place,
seen him handle drugs?


00:59:59.375 --> 01:00:00.924
That rat Rickie has told us.


01:00:01.387 --> 01:00:02.630
He's fuckin dead!


01:00:03.057 --> 01:00:04.397
About 4 weeks ago.


01:00:06.019 --> 01:00:07.019
He's dead.


01:00:07.268 --> 01:00:09.197
Well, we can take him
off the fuckin board.


01:00:09.516 --> 01:00:11.995
I don't think
we got any solid evidence


01:00:12.534 --> 01:00:14.127
on anybody on that board.


01:00:14.516 --> 01:00:17.137
What you saying?
This is weeks and weeks of work, man.


01:00:17.557 --> 01:00:20.389
I say take it down.
We start again from the street.


01:00:23.235 --> 01:00:26.007
That's considerably more
than one year's salary.


01:00:27.787 --> 01:00:29.098
If it disappears...


01:00:29.757 --> 01:00:31.602
we'll not be able
to get it for you again.


01:00:33.289 --> 01:00:34.467
That's yours.


01:00:34.679 --> 01:00:36.429
Sign on my life for you again?


01:00:37.053 --> 01:00:38.653
For a lousy twenty grand?


01:00:42.034 --> 01:00:43.516
It has to be Blue Magic, OK?


01:00:44.102 --> 01:00:45.198
It's gonna be Blue.


01:00:45.876 --> 01:00:48.024
- Pick it up here tomorrow.
- $ 20,000.


01:00:48.301 --> 01:00:49.708
Just leave it there.


01:01:04.079 --> 01:01:05.663
- How did it go?
- Good.


01:01:08.045 --> 01:01:09.203
Here he comes.


01:01:09.579 --> 01:01:10.883
- That's him?
- Yeah.


01:01:12.207 --> 01:01:13.242
He's quick.


01:01:25.259 --> 01:01:28.082
- He goes into the City. What do we do?
- Stay with the fuckin money.


01:01:28.307 --> 01:01:29.931
We stay with the money, all right?


01:01:30.121 --> 01:01:31.777
- We can't go there!
- Yes, we can.


01:01:32.058 --> 01:01:34.128
That's 20 grand in there
that I'm responsible for.


01:01:34.311 --> 01:01:37.239
- I ain't losin it, follow the money!
- It's out of our jurisdiction!


01:01:37.503 --> 01:01:39.350
- Follow the money!
- All right!


01:01:54.370 --> 01:01:55.710
He's pulling over.


01:01:55.969 --> 01:01:57.466
All right, here we go.


01:01:58.092 --> 01:01:59.209
Let me out here.


01:02:01.779 --> 01:02:04.512
- Don't disappear, all right?
- I'll circle the block.


01:02:43.205 --> 01:02:44.133
Sit down!


01:02:46.371 --> 01:02:48.074
Happy birthday, gentlemen.
How you doin?


01:02:49.034 --> 01:02:51.585
<i>You're up to something, huh?
He's going bowling.</i>


01:02:53.472 --> 01:02:55.117
Look at that.
Right between the legs.


01:02:55.299 --> 01:02:56.834
- What's in the bag?
- Nothing.


01:02:56.996 --> 01:02:58.042
Get the fuck up!


01:02:58.317 --> 01:03:00.769
<i>- It's my bag.
- Shut the fuck up! What did I tell you?</i>


01:03:01.013 --> 01:03:02.921
<i>- Keep your your head down!
- What you doin?</i>


01:03:03.104 --> 01:03:05.236
<i>- Sit down and shut up!
- Don't you move!</i>


01:03:18.122 --> 01:03:19.129
Hey guys!


01:03:19.427 --> 01:03:20.662
Guys! Officers!


01:03:22.001 --> 01:03:23.808
I'm Richie Roberts.
Newark.


01:03:26.069 --> 01:03:27.206
That's... my money.


01:03:28.467 --> 01:03:30.337
What the fuck?
What money?


01:03:32.619 --> 01:03:35.086
The bills are sequenced,
they're registered with the Essex


01:03:35.313 --> 01:03:36.741
County Prosecutors Office.


01:03:36.944 --> 01:03:39.655
Check them up.
They all start with CF3500.


01:03:39.922 --> 01:03:40.937
Have a look.


01:03:45.997 --> 01:03:47.162
Fucking registers.


01:03:47.424 --> 01:03:50.139
I thought I had a fucking Chris-Craft
sitting in my driveway.


01:03:50.545 --> 01:03:51.738
Honest mistake.


01:03:52.063 --> 01:03:53.444
I'll just get the money.


01:03:55.205 --> 01:03:56.206
This time.


01:04:00.335 --> 01:04:02.873
When's the last time I was in Jersey?
Let me think.


01:04:05.227 --> 01:04:06.276
Never.


01:04:08.356 --> 01:04:10.448
What’re you doing coming over here
unannounced?


01:04:10.701 --> 01:04:12.706
You know you can get hurt
doing that?


01:04:14.663 --> 01:04:16.403
You got your fucking money.


01:04:16.680 --> 01:04:17.628
Richie.


01:04:18.516 --> 01:04:19.809
And never ever


01:04:20.100 --> 01:04:22.199
come into this city again unannounced.


01:04:22.459 --> 01:04:24.672
You come in to see
a fuckin Broadway show?


01:04:24.964 --> 01:04:27.244
You call ahead first to see
if it’s okay with me.


01:04:29.338 --> 01:04:30.475
No problem.


01:04:35.358 --> 01:04:37.247
- Go hit some ball.
- Great suits.


01:04:40.280 --> 01:04:41.458
Is that your car?


01:04:42.456 --> 01:04:43.662
Fucking great car.


01:04:44.371 --> 01:04:46.570
Have a nice fuckin trip
back to Jersey.


01:04:47.134 --> 01:04:48.154
All right.


01:04:48.467 --> 01:04:50.660
Come on, I got a tea time.
Let's go.


01:05:03.544 --> 01:05:04.945
This is your father?


01:05:06.225 --> 01:05:07.943
That's Martin Luther King.


01:05:08.948 --> 01:05:10.798
- It is not.
- Yes, it is Martin Luther King.


01:05:10.971 --> 01:05:13.438
- You know, "I have a dream".
- Of course.


01:05:13.909 --> 01:05:15.046
No, that's...


01:05:15.849 --> 01:05:18.123
He was just as important
as Martin Luther King.


01:05:18.538 --> 01:05:20.440
- To me.
- What did he do?


01:05:21.523 --> 01:05:24.037
A lot of things, he was a...
friend.


01:05:25.152 --> 01:05:27.284
Served New York,
New York served him.


01:05:28.575 --> 01:05:29.834
He was my boss.


01:05:30.550 --> 01:05:31.544
My teacher.


01:05:32.001 --> 01:05:33.402
What did he teach you?


01:05:33.681 --> 01:05:35.732
He taught me a lot of things. He...


01:05:37.963 --> 01:05:39.871
Taught me how to take my time.


01:05:41.497 --> 01:05:45.114
That if I was going to do something,
to do it with care, love.


01:05:46.335 --> 01:05:47.339
Anything else?


01:05:52.407 --> 01:05:53.890
Taught me to be a gentleman.


01:05:54.603 --> 01:05:55.712
That's what you are?


01:05:55.955 --> 01:05:58.100
That's what I try to be.
Come here.


01:05:59.524 --> 01:06:00.803
Come sit here.


01:06:03.742 --> 01:06:04.798
Look at me.


01:06:05.986 --> 01:06:08.743
I own about five apartments
in Manhattan.


01:06:10.373 --> 01:06:12.955
Homes all over the East Coast.
Could've taken you to anyone of'em,


01:06:13.146 --> 01:06:15.272
but I didn't.
I brought you here.


01:06:15.929 --> 01:06:19.039
- I was looking for you, boy.
- Cause I want you to meet my mother.


01:06:19.479 --> 01:06:20.779
How you doin, Ma?


01:06:21.181 --> 01:06:22.829
- Is this her?
- Eva,


01:06:23.103 --> 01:06:24.524
- this is my mother.
- Hi, Eva.


01:06:25.168 --> 01:06:26.433
Nice to meet you.


01:06:26.633 --> 01:06:27.939
She's beautiful.


01:06:28.606 --> 01:06:29.690
Look at her.


01:06:29.985 --> 01:06:31.274
She's an angel


01:06:31.559 --> 01:06:33.175
come down from Heaven.


01:06:33.636 --> 01:06:34.655
Thank you.


01:06:42.817 --> 01:06:43.826
Mr. Roberts.


01:06:44.435 --> 01:06:46.108
I'm here for our appointment.


01:06:50.578 --> 01:06:51.974
- Morning.
- Morning.


01:06:54.337 --> 01:06:56.043
Sorry, our appointment?


01:06:56.654 --> 01:06:58.130
Child Social Services.


01:07:12.851 --> 01:07:14.821
She did mention your name though.


01:07:15.913 --> 01:07:18.532
- The stewardess?
- No, not her.


01:07:19.767 --> 01:07:22.451
The lady from Social Services,
she mentioned your name.


01:07:23.415 --> 01:07:25.091
Right after she asked me


01:07:25.283 --> 01:07:27.415
if I associated with any criminals.


01:07:27.591 --> 01:07:29.406
- All right, go!
- You want to see this?


01:07:29.846 --> 01:07:30.890
Hey, boys!


01:07:31.620 --> 01:07:32.690
Joey!


01:07:33.535 --> 01:07:34.794
Get in the pool.


01:07:36.333 --> 01:07:37.388
Come on!


01:07:42.700 --> 01:07:44.202
How'd she get my name?


01:07:44.500 --> 01:07:45.550
Laurie.


01:07:47.005 --> 01:07:48.887
She's been saying a lot lately.


01:07:50.194 --> 01:07:51.229
A lot.


01:07:55.267 --> 01:07:57.645
When you asked me to be
your son's godfather,


01:07:57.799 --> 01:07:59.464
- I took it very seriously.
- I know.


01:07:59.761 --> 01:08:01.082
And I appreciate that.


01:08:01.279 --> 01:08:03.974
And I said yes, I would take on
that responsability


01:08:04.261 --> 01:08:06.849
to take care of your son, if God forbid,
something happened to you.


01:08:07.026 --> 01:08:09.601
Jo, the things she said
to Child Social Services


01:08:09.762 --> 01:08:11.280
make me look really bad.


01:08:11.527 --> 01:08:12.397
You know.


01:08:12.750 --> 01:08:14.628
All kinds at the house at night time,


01:08:14.851 --> 01:08:17.166
low life informants around.
Women...


01:08:17.491 --> 01:08:18.831
Old friends like me.


01:08:19.947 --> 01:08:21.486
Old friends like you, yeah.


01:08:23.867 --> 01:08:25.694
Uncle Joey!
Watch me!


01:08:29.717 --> 01:08:30.834
I understand.


01:08:31.101 --> 01:08:33.618
They ask me, I'll tell them
what you want me to tell.


01:08:33.880 --> 01:08:35.830
- I'll lie for you.
- Don't lie.


01:08:36.123 --> 01:08:37.321
You don't have to lie.


01:08:37.554 --> 01:08:40.356
Just... omit certain details.


01:08:41.243 --> 01:08:42.441
Sure, all right.


01:08:45.433 --> 01:08:47.423
I have something else to ask you.


01:08:47.685 --> 01:08:50.041
You don't have to answer
if you don't want.


01:08:52.975 --> 01:08:54.031
Blue Magic.


01:08:54.360 --> 01:08:55.375
Anything?


01:08:56.970 --> 01:09:00.706
A lot of sorrow, misery from guys
getting put out of work. That's all.


01:09:02.883 --> 01:09:04.172
What, your guys?


01:09:04.744 --> 01:09:05.723
His guys.


01:09:07.129 --> 01:09:09.024
You know where it's comin from?


01:09:10.088 --> 01:09:12.333
Guys down south,
that's all I heard.


01:09:13.270 --> 01:09:14.786
- Cubans?
- I dunno.


01:09:16.185 --> 01:09:17.256
Or Mexico?


01:09:18.004 --> 01:09:19.060
Don't know.


01:09:19.676 --> 01:09:21.849
You're telling me
it's from South America?


01:09:22.029 --> 01:09:23.066
I don't know!


01:09:24.350 --> 01:09:28.211
Whoever it is, they're upsetting
the natural order of things.


01:09:29.388 --> 01:09:30.525
That's all there is.


01:09:46.712 --> 01:09:48.205
<i>- What's up?
- My man.</i>


01:09:48.497 --> 01:09:49.507
<i>How's it lookin?</i>


01:11:19.030 --> 01:11:20.614
I want you to meet Mike Sobota.


01:11:20.966 --> 01:11:22.448
- How're you doing?
- How're you?


01:11:22.631 --> 01:11:24.806
- What can I get you?
- A left hander, Charlie told me


01:11:24.965 --> 01:11:26.427
- about your nephew.
- Oh, Mr...


01:11:26.630 --> 01:11:28.864
- Yankees.
- Yeah, yeah! Hey, Steve!


01:11:29.181 --> 01:11:30.476
- Come here.
- Excuse me.


01:11:30.638 --> 01:11:33.247
He's good. Put him in the team.
You're good enough, right?


01:11:33.790 --> 01:11:35.943
I'm a Lucas.
Good enough on a bad day.


01:11:36.144 --> 01:11:38.964
So don't make it a bad day,
make it a good day, you understand?


01:11:40.498 --> 01:11:43.320
Excuse me. Police department.
Now back out, baby.


01:11:46.838 --> 01:11:48.219
I'll take your ass in, Jimmy.


01:11:48.635 --> 01:11:50.381
You can't take me in for that.


01:11:50.943 --> 01:11:52.839
I got a licence for that, motherfucker.


01:11:53.504 --> 01:11:55.681
You got a licence for this?
Excuse me, all right?


01:11:58.571 --> 01:11:59.801
Shit, all right!


01:12:01.361 --> 01:12:03.788
I got to arrest you.
Shit's too good to be on the street.


01:12:04.963 --> 01:12:07.300
- What you doin, man?
- You ain't arresting nobody.


01:12:07.778 --> 01:12:09.316
You bribing me now?


01:12:09.724 --> 01:12:13.215
I tell you what,
I'm arresting everybody. All of you.


01:12:13.570 --> 01:12:14.663
You first!


01:12:19.588 --> 01:12:21.849
- How can that be?
- What was that?


01:12:22.100 --> 01:12:24.091
Get this fuckin...
what's the matter with you?


01:12:24.307 --> 01:12:25.639
- What was that?
- What?


01:12:25.935 --> 01:12:28.824
- What the hell's wrong with you?
- What's your fuckin problem?


01:12:33.967 --> 01:12:35.366
I just shot him in the leg.


01:12:35.834 --> 01:12:36.869
Damn, Jimmy!


01:12:38.499 --> 01:12:39.535
Get up!


01:12:53.459 --> 01:12:54.693
Everybody, get out!


01:12:55.021 --> 01:12:56.091
Get out!


01:12:57.436 --> 01:13:00.062
- Frank, it was an accident.
- Wasn't no goddamn accident.


01:13:00.488 --> 01:13:03.360
He don't feel shit cause he's coked up
all the motherfuckin time!


01:13:04.253 --> 01:13:06.165
He's your driver,
get rid of him.


01:13:06.455 --> 01:13:07.655
He's your cousin!


01:13:07.837 --> 01:13:09.568
He ain't shit to me,
he means nothin.


01:13:09.741 --> 01:13:12.116
- What'll he do, go back home?
- I don't give a damn!


01:13:12.344 --> 01:13:13.424
Send his ass home!


01:13:14.446 --> 01:13:16.415
Don't rub on that.
You'd block that.


01:13:16.697 --> 01:13:20.394
You understand?
That's alpaga, $25,000 alpaga.


01:13:20.586 --> 01:13:23.668
You'd block that shit.
Don't rub, put club soda on it.


01:13:25.773 --> 01:13:27.016
Listen, from now on,


01:13:27.231 --> 01:13:29.220
don't nobody talk to me directly,
understand?


01:13:29.403 --> 01:13:30.711
You got business with me,


01:13:30.934 --> 01:13:33.095
you talk to Huey,
Huey talks to me, got it?


01:13:33.307 --> 01:13:35.715
- All right.
- Never on the phone, got it?


01:13:36.930 --> 01:13:39.245
And take them
goddamn sunglasses off!


01:13:39.566 --> 01:13:42.247
- Take the goddamn sunglasses off!
- Damn it, man!


01:13:45.385 --> 01:13:47.402
Simple-minded ass motherfuckers.


01:14:03.006 --> 01:14:04.777
The whole place was imported


01:14:05.929 --> 01:14:07.147
brick by brick.


01:14:08.536 --> 01:14:09.612
Gloucestershire.


01:14:10.849 --> 01:14:12.649
- Who?
- Quite famous.


01:14:13.633 --> 01:14:14.648
Yours.


01:14:19.809 --> 01:14:20.819
Here you go.


01:14:25.937 --> 01:14:26.992
Pull!


01:14:32.559 --> 01:14:33.630
Come, Eva.


01:14:35.206 --> 01:14:37.947
I'm sure you're dying to see
the rest of the house.


01:14:41.857 --> 01:14:43.816
Of course. Excuse me.


01:14:45.606 --> 01:14:48.327
Thank you for a wonderful lunch.
It was delicious.


01:14:52.290 --> 01:14:54.178
What do you think of monopolies?


01:14:55.960 --> 01:14:58.266
- You mean, like the game?
- No, I just think


01:14:58.608 --> 01:15:00.798
monopolies are made illegal
in the country, Frank,


01:15:00.986 --> 01:15:02.901
cause no one wants to compete.


01:15:03.219 --> 01:15:05.974
Nobody wants to compete,
not with a monopoly.


01:15:06.410 --> 01:15:07.932
Let the dairy farmers do that,


01:15:09.214 --> 01:15:11.213
half of them'd
go out of business tomorrow.


01:15:11.381 --> 01:15:14.142
- I’m just trying to make a living.
- It's your right.


01:15:14.851 --> 01:15:16.887
Everybody's right. It's America.


01:15:17.709 --> 01:15:21.201
We just can't do it
at the unreasonable expense of others.


01:15:22.353 --> 01:15:24.221
Cause it becomes un-American.


01:15:24.460 --> 01:15:26.613
That's why the price we pay
for that gallon of milk


01:15:26.897 --> 01:15:28.687
never represents the true cost
of production


01:15:28.830 --> 01:15:31.287
cause it's gotta be controlled.
It's gotta be set.


01:15:31.828 --> 01:15:32.885
It's gotta be fair.


01:15:33.078 --> 01:15:35.464
Controlled by who?
I set a price I think is fair.


01:15:35.627 --> 01:15:37.175
- I don't think it is.
- You don't?


01:15:37.338 --> 01:15:38.333
I don't.


01:15:38.515 --> 01:15:40.613
I know your customers
are happy, Frank.


01:15:40.810 --> 01:15:43.104
Bunch of fuckin junkies
that they are.


01:15:43.591 --> 01:15:45.765
What about your fellow dairy farmers?


01:15:46.738 --> 01:15:48.148
Are you thinking of us?


01:15:48.871 --> 01:15:50.254
You thinking of them?


01:15:50.807 --> 01:15:52.127
The dairy farmers?


01:15:52.814 --> 01:15:56.692
I'm thinking of them, Dominic, about
as much as they've thought about me.


01:15:57.646 --> 01:15:59.256
I'm just thinking out loud.


01:16:00.626 --> 01:16:02.762
If you took some of your inventory,


01:16:03.342 --> 01:16:05.027
and you sold it wholesale.


01:16:06.867 --> 01:16:09.642
Sit.
We could work.


01:16:10.535 --> 01:16:12.342
You could use some distribution.


01:16:13.604 --> 01:16:16.780
I dunno, I'm pretty good.
I got 110th to 155th,


01:16:17.045 --> 01:16:18.568
river to river, I'm all right.


01:16:19.019 --> 01:16:21.991
It's kind of a mom and pop store
next to what I’m talking about,


01:16:22.245 --> 01:16:23.859
and that's bigger than K-Mart.


01:16:24.026 --> 01:16:26.889
I'm talking about L.A.,
Chicago, Detroit, Las Vegas.


01:16:27.158 --> 01:16:28.620
Let's go nationwide.


01:16:29.272 --> 01:16:31.729
I'm gonna guarantee you
peace of mind here.


01:16:32.303 --> 01:16:33.620
You don't want that?


01:16:34.871 --> 01:16:36.252
You gonna need it.


01:16:37.056 --> 01:16:38.687
I don't know how you feel me.


01:16:38.918 --> 01:16:40.705
I'm kind of a Renaissance man.


01:16:40.901 --> 01:16:42.729
The people I deal with on a daily basis,


01:16:42.962 --> 01:16:44.751
they're not enlightened.


01:16:45.012 --> 01:16:47.428
You talk to them about civil rights,
they don't know.


01:16:47.654 --> 01:16:48.994
They're not open to change.


01:16:49.452 --> 01:16:52.132
Not from the way things are done,
and who's doing it.


01:16:53.180 --> 01:16:55.994
I can talk to them,
so there's no misunderstanding.


01:16:57.964 --> 01:17:00.746
That's what I mean
by peace of mind.


01:17:03.423 --> 01:17:04.432
Here


01:17:05.523 --> 01:17:08.069
You're paying what,
75, 80 thousand a kilo?


01:17:10.912 --> 01:17:12.639
I'm a Renaissance man too.


01:17:14.141 --> 01:17:15.704
I'd consider 50,000.


01:17:25.099 --> 01:17:28.378
Why would you trust these people?
And the way they look at you.


01:17:28.525 --> 01:17:30.920
They look at me like it's Xmas
and I'm Santa Claus.


01:17:31.030 --> 01:17:32.946
They look at us like we're the help.


01:17:34.346 --> 01:17:35.856
They work for me, now.


01:17:41.234 --> 01:17:43.371
<i>I predict it when I meet Joe Frazier,</i>


01:17:43.555 --> 01:17:45.729
<i>this will be like a good amateur</i>


01:17:45.876 --> 01:17:47.792
<i>fighting a real professional.</i>


01:17:47.976 --> 01:17:50.444
<i>This will be like a kid
out of the Olympics...</i>


01:17:50.776 --> 01:17:52.581
That's gonna be Ali in three.


01:17:53.686 --> 01:17:55.270
C'mon, cat, you dig it?


01:17:56.633 --> 01:17:59.248
<i>- You're fightin Joe Frazier.
- It's no depth, and besides the point.</i>


01:17:59.396 --> 01:18:00.575
He's on pot, man.


01:18:00.722 --> 01:18:03.153
- Look at Frazier.
- Ali's craftsman, baby.


01:18:03.448 --> 01:18:05.253
<i>- I'll stop you.
- Stop me? You?</i>


01:18:05.364 --> 01:18:06.469
<i>How soon? What round?</i>


01:18:06.616 --> 01:18:08.716
<i>- No, don't let him obligate you.
- 1 to 10.</i>


01:18:08.863 --> 01:18:10.558
<i>You'll be out. I'll win.</i>


01:18:10.853 --> 01:18:13.431
<i>Time out.
March 8, 1971.</i>


01:18:13.837 --> 01:18:17.152
<i>Here we are at Madison Square Garden
for the fight of the century.</i>


01:18:17.336 --> 01:18:20.578
<i>And by anybody's definition,
this is a happening.</i>


01:18:20.799 --> 01:18:22.862
<i>There are handshakes, and of course,</i>


01:18:23.009 --> 01:18:25.036
<i>there are utterly beautiful women.</i>


01:18:25.183 --> 01:18:27.320
<i>But behind the smiles
and the handshakes,</i>


01:18:27.504 --> 01:18:30.156
<i>you can feel the atmosphere
so heavy with tension</i>


01:18:30.304 --> 01:18:31.961
<i>it's almost unbearable.</i>


01:18:32.514 --> 01:18:34.761
<i>Everybody's who's anybody is here.</i>


01:18:35.056 --> 01:18:37.082
<i>Like Sinatra, like Graziano.</i>


01:18:37.229 --> 01:18:40.655
<i>David Roth and Diahann Carroll.
Woody Allen and Diane Keaton.</i>


01:18:40.766 --> 01:18:42.645
<i>The celebrities are pouring in.</i>


01:18:42.939 --> 01:18:45.665
<i>The way you all build it up,
Life Magazine cover,</i>


01:18:45.849 --> 01:18:48.502
<i>Time Magazine,
everybody gives their opinion.</i>


01:18:48.686 --> 01:18:51.117
<i>Joe Louis here says I'll lose.</i>


01:18:51.412 --> 01:18:54.691
<i>When Joe Louis says I'm gonna lose,
I know I feel wonderful.</i>


01:18:55.538 --> 01:18:57.969
<i>Joe Louis always picks the wrong man.</i>


01:19:10.163 --> 01:19:12.963
<i>Float like a butterfly,
sting like a bee!</i>


01:19:13.515 --> 01:19:15.284
Not watching the fight, Bob?


01:19:15.615 --> 01:19:16.905
I'm not into boxing.


01:19:18.452 --> 01:19:19.962
It ain't boxing, kid.


01:19:20.994 --> 01:19:22.136
It's politics.


01:19:25.783 --> 01:19:27.551
I got something for you too.


01:19:31.566 --> 01:19:32.966
A coat? For me?


01:19:35.140 --> 01:19:36.392
Do you like it?


01:19:36.908 --> 01:19:38.860
The coat? Yeah, it's nice.


01:19:42.139 --> 01:19:43.392
What do you think?


01:19:43.539 --> 01:19:44.902
- Yeah.
- You sure?


01:19:53.412 --> 01:19:54.701
Over here, Sammy!


01:19:55.880 --> 01:19:57.427
Hey, Sammy, get'em up!


01:19:59.564 --> 01:20:00.890
Joe Louis, over here!


01:20:01.332 --> 01:20:02.548
How's it goin, Frank?


01:20:13.710 --> 01:20:14.999
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,</i>


01:20:15.220 --> 01:20:17.688
<i>we have quite a list of introductions.</i>


01:20:18.425 --> 01:20:21.004
<i>We are now going to introduce people</i>


01:20:21.409 --> 01:20:23.546
<i>from all endeavors of life.</i>


01:20:23.988 --> 01:20:25.940
<i>And not just show people,</i>


01:20:26.382 --> 01:20:29.514
<i>because everyone's in here tonight.</i>


01:20:33.492 --> 01:20:35.776
Let's go, take your seats now.
C'mon!


01:20:41.486 --> 01:20:42.628
<i>Main event.</i>


01:20:43.218 --> 01:20:45.170
- Here they come!
- Ali!


01:20:45.354 --> 01:20:48.522
<i>Fifteen rounds for the undisputed</i>


01:20:48.928 --> 01:20:49.996
<i>Heavyweight</i>


01:20:50.180 --> 01:20:52.169
<i>Championship of the World!</i>


01:20:52.390 --> 01:20:53.385
Go, Ali!


01:20:53.532 --> 01:20:55.448
<i>From Louisville, Kentucky,</i>


01:20:55.780 --> 01:20:57.585
<i>- he's wearing red trunks.
- Champ!</i>


01:20:57.769 --> 01:21:00.753
<i>- This is Frank Lucas.
- He weighs 213 pounds.</i>


01:21:01.895 --> 01:21:03.663
<i>Here is Muhammad</i>


01:21:04.179 --> 01:21:05.358
<i>Ali!</i>


01:21:06.610 --> 01:21:07.973
<i>His opponent</i>


01:21:08.157 --> 01:21:10.441
<i>from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania,</i>


01:21:11.399 --> 01:21:13.204
<i>he's wearing green trunks.</i>


01:21:13.831 --> 01:21:15.857
Who's that laughing with Cattano?


01:21:16.557 --> 01:21:18.325
How'd he get
so fuckin close to the ring?


01:21:18.509 --> 01:21:19.688
<i>The heavyweight</i>


01:21:19.946 --> 01:21:21.567
champion of the world,


01:21:21.972 --> 01:21:24.845
<i>Joe Frazier!</i>


01:21:29.156 --> 01:21:31.734
You gonna keep that hat on all night?
I'll miss the fight.


01:21:31.918 --> 01:21:32.987
You paid for it.


01:21:37.407 --> 01:21:38.623
Joe, over here!


01:22:19.035 --> 01:22:20.988
<i>This guy's a supplier at most,
or just a pimp.</i>


01:22:21.135 --> 01:22:23.935
<i>- Otherwise we'd know about him.
- His tickets were phenomenal.</i>


01:22:24.119 --> 01:22:25.998
Better seats than Dominic Cattano.


01:22:26.624 --> 01:22:28.245
Joe Louis shook his hand.


01:22:29.718 --> 01:22:31.413
Who the fuck is this guy?


01:22:35.465 --> 01:22:36.607
What's this?


01:22:36.976 --> 01:22:39.075
That's the plate of the limo.


01:22:39.333 --> 01:22:41.507
Check with the company
who rented it.


01:22:44.822 --> 01:22:46.959
Right there, Mr. Lucas!
Right there.


01:22:49.353 --> 01:22:50.532
Picture here!


01:22:51.932 --> 01:22:53.406
Looking good, Frank!


01:22:58.932 --> 01:23:00.479
Congratulations!


01:23:06.189 --> 01:23:08.252
She's the most beautiful bride
I've ever seen.


01:23:08.362 --> 01:23:10.352
That's my sunshine right there,
Mr. Williams.


01:23:10.646 --> 01:23:12.304
I wish Bumpy could’ve met her.


01:23:18.309 --> 01:23:19.561
Get a picture.


01:23:29.139 --> 01:23:30.944
Now come here, baby.


01:23:56.032 --> 01:23:58.021
- What's happening?
- Sit tight.


01:23:59.642 --> 01:24:01.042
Congratulations, Frank.


01:24:02.184 --> 01:24:03.326
Detective.


01:24:03.694 --> 01:24:06.273
You're sure you did the right thing?
I mean, she's a beautiful


01:24:06.531 --> 01:24:08.962
- girl and all. Don't get me wrong.
- Hey, listen.


01:24:10.104 --> 01:24:11.983
Before you say anything
about me or my wife,


01:24:12.167 --> 01:24:14.230
understand this is
the most important day of my life.


01:24:14.893 --> 01:24:16.293
I understand,


01:24:16.588 --> 01:24:19.093
a man walks around in a $50,000
chinchilla coat


01:24:19.240 --> 01:24:21.229
and never even bought me
a cup of coffee...


01:24:21.524 --> 01:24:23.255
there's something wrong there.


01:24:23.697 --> 01:24:25.245
You pay your bills, Frank?


01:24:26.092 --> 01:24:28.044
- Don't know what you're sayin.
- Pay your bills?


01:24:28.192 --> 01:24:30.991
If you're not getting your share,
you should go talk to your chief.


01:24:31.102 --> 01:24:34.270
What's my share?
Cause you don't fuckin know me.


01:24:35.265 --> 01:24:37.954
- Maybe I am special.
- You are special.


01:24:38.580 --> 01:24:40.238
Do you see that right there?


01:24:40.570 --> 01:24:42.964
Special Investigations Unit.


01:24:43.848 --> 01:24:44.953
Special.


01:24:45.948 --> 01:24:47.016
Get it?


01:24:48.085 --> 01:24:50.553
Ten grand, first of each month,


01:24:50.737 --> 01:24:52.284
deliver right here.


01:24:53.132 --> 01:24:55.195
- Are you done?
- Yeah, I'm done.


01:24:58.694 --> 01:25:01.420
Don't forget your card.
Have a fuckin nice honeymoon.


01:25:01.752 --> 01:25:02.783
Let's go.


01:26:02.794 --> 01:26:04.599
<i>His name is Frank Lucas,</i>


01:26:04.746 --> 01:26:07.472
originally from Greensboro,
North Carolina.


01:26:07.619 --> 01:26:12.335
Couple of arrests years ago,
gambling and unlicensed firearm.


01:26:12.887 --> 01:26:15.319
For fifteen years,
he was Bumpy Johnson's driver.


01:26:15.613 --> 01:26:17.382
Bodyguard and collector.


01:26:19.003 --> 01:26:20.660
He was with him when he died.


01:26:20.881 --> 01:26:22.429
He's got five brothers.


01:26:22.797 --> 01:26:24.013
He's the oldest.


01:26:24.381 --> 01:26:26.186
And a lot of cousins.


01:26:26.849 --> 01:26:28.102
They all live up here now,


01:26:28.286 --> 01:26:30.128
spread throughout
the five boroughs in Jersey.


01:26:31.123 --> 01:26:32.633
The brothers are Dexter,


01:26:33.296 --> 01:26:35.470
<i>- What can I do for you?
- In Brooklyn, a dry cleaner.</i>


01:26:35.617 --> 01:26:36.612
Picking up.


01:26:38.490 --> 01:26:41.658
<i>Melvin in Queens has a custom
furniture and fire door business.</i>


01:26:43.832 --> 01:26:45.305
- This one here?
- Right there.


01:26:45.453 --> 01:26:47.700
<i>Terrence in Newark
has a hardware store.</i>


01:26:49.210 --> 01:26:51.568
<i>Turner in the Bronx has a tire shop.</i>


01:26:53.373 --> 01:26:55.952
<i>And Huey Lucas in Bergen County
has a body shop.</i>


01:26:56.247 --> 01:26:57.425
Is there a manager here?


01:26:57.646 --> 01:26:59.636
- That's my price.
- I'll take it somewhere else.


01:26:59.894 --> 01:27:03.135
<i>These businesses are the distribution
and collection points</i>


01:27:03.320 --> 01:27:05.714
<i>for Frank's dope,
and Frank's money.</i>


01:27:06.340 --> 01:27:09.472
Everything about Frank's life
seems unpretentious,


01:27:10.135 --> 01:27:11.682
<i>orderly and legitimate.</i>


01:27:12.566 --> 01:27:14.334
<i>Starts early, gets up at 5 am.</i>


01:27:15.071 --> 01:27:17.245
<i>Has breakfast in a diner in Harlem
every morning</i>


01:27:17.503 --> 01:27:19.860
<i>usually by himself.
Then starts work.</i>


01:27:20.339 --> 01:27:23.397
<i>Takes a meeting with the accountant,
or his lawyer.</i>


01:27:23.655 --> 01:27:25.644
<i>At night, he usually stays at home,</i>


01:27:25.754 --> 01:27:26.970
<i>and if he does go out,</i>


01:27:27.265 --> 01:27:30.175
<i>it's to one of two clubs, or a handful
of restaurants with his new wife.</i>


01:27:31.280 --> 01:27:33.564
<i>Ball players, friends</i>


01:27:33.785 --> 01:27:36.695
<i>musicians, never, never,
organized crime guys.</i>


01:27:37.580 --> 01:27:39.827
<i>Sundays,
he takes his mother to church.</i>


01:27:40.821 --> 01:27:42.811
<i>Then he drives out
and he changes the flowers</i>


01:27:43.032 --> 01:27:46.163
on Bumpy's grave.
Every Sunday no matter what.


01:27:47.195 --> 01:27:48.668
<i>Not your typical day in the life</i>


01:27:48.852 --> 01:27:50.178
<i>of a dope man, Richie.</i>


01:27:51.468 --> 01:27:54.304
<i>Bumpy's life wasn't typical either,
and he ran Harlem for years.</i>


01:27:55.410 --> 01:27:58.504
<i>You're saying that Frank Lucas
replaced Bumpy Johnson?</i>


01:27:59.020 --> 01:28:00.493
<i>- Yeah.
- His driver?</i>


01:28:01.304 --> 01:28:03.035
Sounds a little far-fetched.


01:28:03.330 --> 01:28:05.945
<i>But is it?
Because everything he does...</i>


01:28:06.166 --> 01:28:07.235
<i>Handing out turkeys.</i>


01:28:07.382 --> 01:28:09.592
<i>He does the same
as Bumpy would've done.</i>


01:28:09.777 --> 01:28:11.545
<i>Who was Bumpy most likely to teach?</i>


01:28:12.834 --> 01:28:14.345
The guy he sees every day.


01:28:15.192 --> 01:28:16.997
<i>It's like a Sicilian family.</i>


01:28:17.660 --> 01:28:19.576
He structured his organization


01:28:19.723 --> 01:28:21.418
to protect him in the same way.


01:28:21.602 --> 01:28:23.149
And if he was with Bumpy for so long,


01:28:23.296 --> 01:28:25.728
that means he would've spent
a lot of time with Italians,


01:28:25.912 --> 01:28:28.159
definitively long enough
to learn that much.


01:28:28.712 --> 01:28:30.185
But here's the thing.


01:28:30.443 --> 01:28:32.911
I don't think it's Frank Lucas
we're after.


01:28:33.132 --> 01:28:35.932
Who we want
is whoever Lucas is working for.


01:28:36.227 --> 01:28:38.142
Whoever is bringing the heroin in.


01:28:38.290 --> 01:28:39.284
Okay.


01:28:40.353 --> 01:28:43.742
So, what do you have on him
that'll stick in court?


01:28:43.926 --> 01:28:45.400
Because this isn't it.


01:28:46.431 --> 01:28:48.531
Without powder,
without informants,


01:28:49.047 --> 01:28:50.483
no one's going to jail.


01:28:50.741 --> 01:28:53.062
That's understood, Sir,
I don't think we'll get


01:28:53.320 --> 01:28:55.309
informants,
not from inside the family.


01:28:55.567 --> 01:28:58.220
Unless we get very, very lucky.


01:29:06.914 --> 01:29:08.129
That's it down there.


01:29:54.399 --> 01:29:55.835
Let's all join hands.


01:29:59.924 --> 01:30:01.693
Lord, we thank you for this food


01:30:01.840 --> 01:30:04.492
we're about to receive
the nourishment of our bodies.


01:30:04.713 --> 01:30:06.666
Fill our souls with heavenly grace,


01:30:06.887 --> 01:30:09.245
in Jesus' name, and for his sake.


01:30:09.576 --> 01:30:11.455
- Amen.
- Amen!


01:30:32.490 --> 01:30:33.632
It's OK.


01:30:34.332 --> 01:30:35.363
Come on.


01:30:36.542 --> 01:30:37.684
It's OK.


01:30:38.752 --> 01:30:41.847
- Better ready yourself.
- C'mon, big man, throw the ball.


01:30:42.363 --> 01:30:44.057
- C'mon.
- Get yourself ready, ol' man.


01:30:45.126 --> 01:30:46.562
C'mon, now.


01:30:47.336 --> 01:30:48.367
C'mon, now.


01:30:48.588 --> 01:30:50.799
I'm going to set your ass
in the grass, Uncle Melvin.


01:30:51.130 --> 01:30:53.451
Watch your mouth, boy,
and throw the ball.


01:30:53.746 --> 01:30:56.251
Damn, Uncle Melvin,
I gonna pitch that out field.


01:30:57.503 --> 01:30:58.535
Come here.


01:30:59.972 --> 01:31:01.077
Sit down.


01:31:01.261 --> 01:31:02.292
Uncle Frank.


01:31:02.808 --> 01:31:03.913
What's happenin?


01:31:04.245 --> 01:31:05.276
How you doin?


01:31:05.645 --> 01:31:06.676
Cool.


01:31:06.897 --> 01:31:07.929
Want a drink?


01:31:08.223 --> 01:31:10.176
- You know better than that.
- Just checking.


01:31:13.676 --> 01:31:15.812
Why didn't you show up
for that meeting?


01:31:17.691 --> 01:31:20.049
I set it up with the Yankees
and Billy Martin.


01:31:22.738 --> 01:31:24.175
Why didn't you show up?


01:31:27.085 --> 01:31:28.227
Don't lie to me.


01:31:29.258 --> 01:31:31.248
I don't want to play ball no more.


01:31:32.242 --> 01:31:35.116
- I decided.
- What you mean, decided what?


01:31:35.742 --> 01:31:37.547
- I don't want it.
- What you talkin about?


01:31:37.694 --> 01:31:39.094
You play since you was little,


01:31:39.278 --> 01:31:41.047
you're ready for the pros,
what do you...


01:31:42.262 --> 01:31:43.441
We got a problem.


01:31:46.683 --> 01:31:47.825
What do you want?


01:31:49.814 --> 01:31:51.656
I want what you got, Uncle Frank.


01:31:52.393 --> 01:31:53.425
I want to be you.


01:32:37.557 --> 01:32:38.626
My man!


01:32:40.725 --> 01:32:42.641
- Welcome, Frank.
- How you doin, Nick?


01:32:43.120 --> 01:32:44.667
It's all great, welcome.


01:32:45.625 --> 01:32:47.688
- I need to talk to you.
- Right, c'mon.


01:32:50.451 --> 01:32:52.809
Yeah, everybody's good,
everybody's happy,


01:32:53.030 --> 01:32:55.535
Charlie, Baz, the Italians,
johnny law,


01:32:55.719 --> 01:32:57.377
everybody's happy except you.


01:32:57.929 --> 01:33:00.176
I don't get why you have
to take something that's


01:33:00.397 --> 01:33:01.650
perfectly good,


01:33:02.387 --> 01:33:03.492
and mess it up.


01:33:04.339 --> 01:33:05.444
See, brand name,


01:33:05.628 --> 01:33:07.765
brand name means something,
you understand?


01:33:07.912 --> 01:33:09.165
Shut the fuck up!


01:33:10.491 --> 01:33:12.628
Go ahead.
Sorry about that bullshit.


01:33:13.843 --> 01:33:14.985
Blue Magic.


01:33:15.870 --> 01:33:17.012
That's a brand name.


01:33:17.269 --> 01:33:19.222
Like Pepsi, that's a brand name.


01:33:19.480 --> 01:33:21.837
I stand behind it, I guarantee it.


01:33:22.132 --> 01:33:23.864
They know that even if
they don't know me


01:33:24.121 --> 01:33:26.921
any more than
the chairman of General Mills.


01:33:27.216 --> 01:33:30.200
- What the fuck you talkin about?
- What I'm talking about is when you


01:33:30.310 --> 01:33:33.110
chop my dope down
to 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 %,


01:33:33.294 --> 01:33:35.652
and then call it
Blue Magic,


01:33:36.315 --> 01:33:38.783
that's trademark infringement,
understand?


01:33:39.741 --> 01:33:42.172
With all due respect,
if I buy something I own it.


01:33:42.357 --> 01:33:43.388
That ain't true.


01:33:43.536 --> 01:33:45.893
I buy a car,
I can paint the motherfucker.


01:33:46.077 --> 01:33:48.325
But you don't have to,
that's what I'm saying to you,


01:33:48.435 --> 01:33:51.051
it's good enough the way it is.
You can make enough money of it


01:33:51.198 --> 01:33:53.150
the way it is
just by calling it Blue Magic.


01:33:53.261 --> 01:33:54.845
More than that is greed, son!


01:33:55.066 --> 01:33:56.982
What you want?
That I change the name?


01:33:57.129 --> 01:33:59.155
I'd have to insist
that you change the name.


01:33:59.376 --> 01:34:00.444
Fine by me,


01:34:00.666 --> 01:34:01.844
I'll call it Red Magic.


01:34:01.992 --> 01:34:04.276
- Even if it don't sound as good.
- Name it what you want.


01:34:04.423 --> 01:34:06.081
Put a choker on it, motherfucker,


01:34:06.228 --> 01:34:08.733
and call it Blue Dogshit,
know what I mean?


01:34:08.917 --> 01:34:10.980
Just don't let me
catch you doing this again.


01:34:13.338 --> 01:34:15.659
"Catch me",
"infringement", "insist"?


01:34:16.138 --> 01:34:18.606
I don't like these words
as much as "please",


01:34:18.938 --> 01:34:20.779
"thank you, sorry to bother you Nicky,"


01:34:20.927 --> 01:34:23.948
these are better words to use
when you come to my club uninvited.


01:34:24.095 --> 01:34:25.126
Hear me?


01:34:26.674 --> 01:34:27.705
My man.


01:34:36.399 --> 01:34:37.467
Shit.


01:34:38.204 --> 01:34:39.641
Fuck, is that cops there?


01:34:48.666 --> 01:34:49.698
It's all right.


01:34:51.245 --> 01:34:53.308
What the hell they gonna do,
give us a ticket?


01:34:54.266 --> 01:34:55.924
Stuff's in the car, Frank.


01:34:58.576 --> 01:35:00.713
- What?
- Some of it is in the trunk.


01:35:03.476 --> 01:35:06.238
- How you doin, Frank?
- Good, how was your Thanksgiving?


01:35:06.902 --> 01:35:09.259
Not so good as a matter of fact.
Get out of the car.


01:35:15.006 --> 01:35:17.032
- Give me the keys.
- Where's the Shelby at?


01:35:17.253 --> 01:35:19.574
It's gone. Stay right there.


01:35:19.795 --> 01:35:21.121
Yes, sir, right here.


01:35:22.705 --> 01:35:24.326
Got anything worth lookin at?


01:35:24.805 --> 01:35:26.131
That's the Trupo guy.


01:35:26.389 --> 01:35:27.789
- Is that him?
- Yeah.


01:35:28.268 --> 01:35:29.447
Fuckin prick.


01:35:32.689 --> 01:35:34.199
Come here a minute, Frank.


01:35:36.962 --> 01:35:38.288
What we gonna do about this?


01:35:38.841 --> 01:35:41.788
Nothing, close it up, throw it back in,
everybody go home.


01:35:42.083 --> 01:35:43.814
Have some pumpkin pie,
warm apple cider.


01:35:44.109 --> 01:35:45.693
I got a better idea.


01:35:46.687 --> 01:35:49.266
Or would you rather me
throw you and your bro in the river?


01:35:50.150 --> 01:35:52.287
Or would you rather
your house blows up next time?


01:35:57.776 --> 01:35:59.691
- I loved that car.
- I know.


01:36:03.338 --> 01:36:04.444
What's he doin?


01:36:04.812 --> 01:36:05.991
Shakedown.


01:36:06.691 --> 01:36:09.233
Somebody's getting some money
for the benevolent funk.


01:36:10.780 --> 01:36:11.922
Sorry, Frank.


01:36:12.143 --> 01:36:13.506
Go on, get in the car.


01:36:37.893 --> 01:36:39.477
All right, you call me back.


01:36:41.688 --> 01:36:43.308
INS, IRS, FBI,


01:36:43.530 --> 01:36:45.482
can't get a damn thing out of them.


01:36:45.666 --> 01:36:47.840
Cause they all think
you're on the take.


01:36:48.945 --> 01:36:50.345
And you think they are.


01:36:51.266 --> 01:36:53.255
I don't think they want this to stop.


01:36:54.213 --> 01:36:55.944
He employs too many people.


01:36:56.681 --> 01:37:00.365
Judges, lawyers, cops,
politicians, prison guards,


01:37:00.917 --> 01:37:02.391
probation officers.


01:37:03.680 --> 01:37:06.996
His dope stops flowing in, a hundred
thousand people lose their job.


01:37:19.410 --> 01:37:20.958
What the fuck is a microwave?


01:37:21.179 --> 01:37:24.457
It's a scientific force,
like atomic energy.


01:37:26.520 --> 01:37:28.510
It rearranges the molecules.


01:37:28.841 --> 01:37:30.388
- Of what?
- Of what...


01:37:30.683 --> 01:37:31.678
Of popcorn.


01:37:34.441 --> 01:37:36.909
Of your head.
Stick it in, go on.


01:37:40.187 --> 01:37:41.882
I can get you one of those.


01:37:42.361 --> 01:37:43.871
Brand new, just like this.


01:37:44.240 --> 01:37:45.676
I'll have it delivered.


01:37:45.971 --> 01:37:47.260
No, thank you.


01:37:58.644 --> 01:38:01.591
- Where is that?
- Aspen, we just got back.


01:38:01.849 --> 01:38:04.206
- Great time. You know who we met?
- Who?


01:38:05.643 --> 01:38:06.896
Burt Reynolds.


01:38:09.769 --> 01:38:10.874
I'm not kidding.


01:38:11.500 --> 01:38:14.705
Hollywood people go up there,
they're buying up everything.


01:38:15.516 --> 01:38:16.768
This is your place?


01:38:16.989 --> 01:38:18.279
You know what it’s worth?


01:38:18.500 --> 01:38:20.968
Ski in, ski out,
five bedrooms,


01:38:21.189 --> 01:38:22.552
sauna, everything.


01:38:22.994 --> 01:38:24.320
We were guests.


01:38:28.999 --> 01:38:30.362
It's your place.


01:38:45.797 --> 01:38:47.787
Isn’t there something we can do


01:38:50.144 --> 01:38:51.618
about leaving the big guy alone?


01:38:53.165 --> 01:38:54.491
You know what I mean.


01:38:55.154 --> 01:38:58.470
I don’t report what you just said,
then I can get in a lot of trouble.


01:38:58.801 --> 01:39:00.791
I do report it,
and the trouble is yours.


01:39:03.701 --> 01:39:05.359
Hoping you won't do that.


01:39:06.979 --> 01:39:08.821
C'mon, I am not taping it.


01:39:09.595 --> 01:39:11.805
How do you know?
Because we're friends.


01:39:12.726 --> 01:39:15.858
- I'm telling you, this is a real offer.
- From who?


01:39:16.373 --> 01:39:17.515
Your uncle?


01:39:20.905 --> 01:39:23.336
Why would you do this?
Why risk our friendship?


01:39:23.594 --> 01:39:24.773
Because...


01:39:27.167 --> 01:39:28.899
I care what happens to you.


01:39:31.404 --> 01:39:33.061
You shouldn’t have done it.


01:39:33.798 --> 01:39:36.672
I had too, I had no choice,
neither do you, Richie!


01:39:37.482 --> 01:39:39.471
You don't have a choice!
Just leave


01:39:39.913 --> 01:39:41.461
Frank Lucas alone!


01:39:42.897 --> 01:39:44.039
Frank Lucas?


01:39:49.418 --> 01:39:51.628
Tell Maria I had to leave,
I'm sorry.


01:39:53.028 --> 01:39:54.133
Tell her why.


01:40:37.345 --> 01:40:38.745
- Talk!
- Don't shoot!


01:40:38.966 --> 01:40:40.771
- Are you Richie Roberts?
- Yes, so what?


01:40:42.134 --> 01:40:43.902
It's been served.
Sorry.


01:41:03.832 --> 01:41:04.863
Laurie.


01:41:07.037 --> 01:41:09.837
I'm sorry I never gave you
the kind of life you wanted.


01:41:10.868 --> 01:41:12.710
I'm sorry it was never enough.


01:41:16.283 --> 01:41:18.273
Don't punish me for being honest.


01:41:19.157 --> 01:41:20.667
Don't take my boy away.


01:41:23.320 --> 01:41:24.830
What? Are you saying...


01:41:25.272 --> 01:41:26.709
that because you were honest


01:41:26.893 --> 01:41:29.287
and didn't take money
like every other cop, I left you?


01:41:30.061 --> 01:41:31.314
No, you don't take money


01:41:31.571 --> 01:41:32.677
for one reason.


01:41:32.861 --> 01:41:35.550
To buy being dishonest
about everything else.


01:41:35.992 --> 01:41:38.313
It's worse than taking money
nobody gives a shit about!


01:41:38.534 --> 01:41:41.223
Drug money, gambling money
nobody's gonna miss.


01:41:41.518 --> 01:41:44.760
I'd rather you took it
and been honest with me!


01:41:45.091 --> 01:41:47.817
Or don't take it, I don't care,
but don't go cheating on me!


01:41:47.965 --> 01:41:50.065
Or on your kid
by never being around.


01:41:50.175 --> 01:41:52.017
Don't go out and get laid
by your snitches,


01:41:52.238 --> 01:41:54.043
and your secretaries and strippers!


01:41:54.227 --> 01:41:56.474
I can tell by just looking
she's one of'em.


01:41:58.316 --> 01:42:00.895
You think you're going to Heaven
cause you're honest.


01:42:01.153 --> 01:42:02.258
But you're not!


01:42:03.032 --> 01:42:06.237
You're going to the same hell
as the crooked cops you can't stand!


01:42:06.937 --> 01:42:08.115
All rise!


01:42:12.941 --> 01:42:14.415
Please, be seated.


01:42:16.036 --> 01:42:17.215
Ms. Dickerson.


01:42:17.878 --> 01:42:20.125
Before the court renders its opinion,


01:42:20.530 --> 01:42:23.072
is there anything else
you'll like to be heard on?


01:42:23.330 --> 01:42:24.619
Yes, your honor.


01:42:25.172 --> 01:42:27.419
Your Honor, a lot has been said here
today about


01:42:27.566 --> 01:42:30.366
how unsavory Mr. Roberts’
environment is for a child.


01:42:30.845 --> 01:42:32.282
How dangerous it is.


01:42:32.540 --> 01:42:34.271
We tell him to protects us.


01:42:34.566 --> 01:42:36.408
We give him that responsability
but then


01:42:36.629 --> 01:42:38.913
say "Oh, we don’t trust you
to raise a child. "


01:42:39.060 --> 01:42:41.712
- "We don't think you're fit for that. "
- I'm not.


01:42:43.075 --> 01:42:44.144
You're right.


01:42:45.728 --> 01:42:47.864
Being around me
is no place for a kid.


01:42:48.233 --> 01:42:51.290
You take him to Vegas.
I'll come see him when I can.


01:42:54.459 --> 01:42:57.479
Your Honor, I want to apologize
for wasting the court's time.


01:43:09.968 --> 01:43:10.999
Doc.


01:43:11.883 --> 01:43:12.878
I see him.


01:43:13.394 --> 01:43:14.499
Here he is.


01:43:33.397 --> 01:43:34.686
What's going on?


01:43:36.565 --> 01:43:37.634
Champagne?


01:43:37.818 --> 01:43:39.512
- Merry Xmas, detectives!
- For us?


01:43:39.660 --> 01:43:40.839
Yeah, enjoy that.


01:43:41.686 --> 01:43:43.196
Fellas, have a good time.


01:43:45.407 --> 01:43:46.475
Good stuff.


01:43:50.638 --> 01:43:52.885
<i>The South Vietnamese troops
conducted airstrikes</i>


01:43:53.069 --> 01:43:55.464
<i>on communist positions inside the city.</i>


01:43:57.563 --> 01:44:00.032
Paying all of johnny law,
that's one thing.


01:44:00.437 --> 01:44:02.352
I got no problem with that,
I've been...


01:44:02.647 --> 01:44:04.784
paying off the police since I was ten,


01:44:04.968 --> 01:44:07.583
putting more of their kids to college
than the National Merit Award.


01:44:07.768 --> 01:44:09.094
Give me one of them rounded.


01:44:09.389 --> 01:44:11.083
This is different though.


01:44:11.709 --> 01:44:14.030
This Special Investigative Unit,
that's their problem,


01:44:14.214 --> 01:44:16.830
- they think they're special.
- Fucking crooks.


01:44:17.125 --> 01:44:19.188
- No code of ethics.
- What do you think?


01:44:19.446 --> 01:44:21.177
Looks great. It's beautiful.


01:44:21.987 --> 01:44:23.056
Good.


01:44:23.756 --> 01:44:25.782
The police, that's not what
I'm worrying about.


01:44:25.966 --> 01:44:28.066
I'm seeing cars
where I never seen 'em before.


01:44:28.250 --> 01:44:30.423
- People I don't know.
- Yeah, me too.


01:44:34.697 --> 01:44:36.428
- Merry Xmas, Charlie.
- Thank you.


01:44:36.797 --> 01:44:38.639
- I love you.
- I love you too.


01:44:40.738 --> 01:44:41.770
Take this.


01:44:42.838 --> 01:44:44.349
A quick toast and I'll be off.


01:44:52.048 --> 01:44:54.737
- We're gonna have a great time.
- That's right, chica.


01:44:54.884 --> 01:44:56.984
Mr. Lucas.
Enjoy your evening.


01:44:58.421 --> 01:44:59.526
It's all clear.


01:45:05.162 --> 01:45:07.373
<i>- Who is that?
- It's Nicky. You see him?</i>


01:45:07.667 --> 01:45:08.957
Yeah, I see him.


01:45:09.509 --> 01:45:10.725
Just keep going.


01:45:11.388 --> 01:45:12.935
- Around back?
- Hell, no,


01:45:13.156 --> 01:45:14.998
I ain't sneaking in my own club.


01:45:16.030 --> 01:45:17.319
Incredible.


01:45:18.130 --> 01:45:19.382
<i>Increhible.</i>


01:45:40.086 --> 01:45:41.154
Come on.


01:45:44.654 --> 01:45:45.722
Hold on.


01:45:54.011 --> 01:45:55.079
What?


01:45:55.263 --> 01:45:56.773
I want to wait in the car.


01:45:57.031 --> 01:45:58.836
I got it, I'll wait for this.


01:46:00.642 --> 01:46:02.631
- Get that yellow sauce.
- Yellow sauce.


01:46:02.962 --> 01:46:04.878
And the chicken,
the Kung Pao chicken.


01:46:10.956 --> 01:46:12.283
Can you turn the heater on?


01:46:19.061 --> 01:46:21.087
Shit.
I'm gonna go get the keys.


01:46:35.270 --> 01:46:37.259
- Doc, give me the key.
- Here you go.


01:46:43.559 --> 01:46:44.590
Doc!


01:46:48.974 --> 01:46:49.969
Get out!


01:46:57.078 --> 01:46:58.147
You're okay?


01:46:59.215 --> 01:47:00.247
Shit!


01:47:00.725 --> 01:47:02.678
- Come on.
- Are you all right?


01:47:04.594 --> 01:47:05.662
Let's go.


01:47:26.586 --> 01:47:27.802
Was it Nicky?


01:47:29.681 --> 01:47:32.075
We'll go right now fuckin kill him
whether it was or not,


01:47:32.259 --> 01:47:33.843
you say the word, Frankie.


01:47:35.575 --> 01:47:37.196
We got to do something.


01:47:38.338 --> 01:47:40.474
- We can't just sit here.
- We're leaving.


01:47:44.048 --> 01:47:45.669
- Everybody, get out.
- You all right?


01:47:45.890 --> 01:47:48.763
Go on home. It's Xmas time,
you gotta be with your family.


01:47:49.574 --> 01:47:51.305
Go on, be with your kids.


01:48:06.114 --> 01:48:08.767
Where we gonna go?
Spain? Somewhere in China?


01:48:09.614 --> 01:48:11.677
Sit down,
tell me where you want to go.


01:48:14.440 --> 01:48:16.503
We can go anywhere we want.


01:48:16.724 --> 01:48:18.197
- We can live anywhere.
- Where?


01:48:18.382 --> 01:48:19.781
And do what? Run? Hide?


01:48:20.039 --> 01:48:22.286
Frank Lucas don't run
from nobody, baby.


01:48:23.060 --> 01:48:26.597
We ain't going nowhere,
we stay here, this is my home.


01:48:27.333 --> 01:48:29.691
This is where my business is,
my wife, my mother,


01:48:30.096 --> 01:48:32.970
my family, my country.
I ain't going nowhere.


01:48:34.038 --> 01:48:35.696
I am running from nobody.


01:48:37.538 --> 01:48:38.827
This is America.


01:48:46.047 --> 01:48:48.000
And you ain't going away either.


01:48:54.078 --> 01:48:56.289
<i>A ceasefire,
internationally supervised,</i>


01:48:56.546 --> 01:48:58.499
<i>will begin at 7 pm</i>


01:48:58.720 --> 01:49:01.004
<i>this Saturday, January 27,
Washington time.</i>


01:49:01.151 --> 01:49:02.072
Call you back.


01:49:02.256 --> 01:49:04.098
<i>Within 60 days from this saturday...</i>


01:49:04.761 --> 01:49:06.161
What are you doing?


01:49:16.402 --> 01:49:17.250
So...


01:49:17.839 --> 01:49:20.786
From what I hear, a Corsican mob
took a shot at Frank.


01:49:21.192 --> 01:49:23.218
The French Connection, Fernando Rey,


01:49:23.402 --> 01:49:25.686
the exporters
that Frank has put out of business.


01:49:26.975 --> 01:49:28.854
I can take care of him in New York.


01:49:29.480 --> 01:49:32.391
I just don’t want to worry every time
he drives across the bridge to Jersey


01:49:32.538 --> 01:49:34.306
someone’s gonna take
another shot at him.


01:49:36.701 --> 01:49:38.800
You and I gotta start
working together.


01:49:39.169 --> 01:49:41.084
We need to step up our efforts.


01:49:41.895 --> 01:49:43.847
Next time, their aim could be better.


01:49:45.100 --> 01:49:47.421
We need to keep this cash cow alive.


01:49:53.499 --> 01:49:55.304
What the fuck you're doing here?


01:50:00.830 --> 01:50:03.077
You actually gonna arrest Frank Lucas?


01:50:03.593 --> 01:50:06.061
- What's the matter with you?
- What, you don't know?


01:50:07.977 --> 01:50:10.003
Everybody in New Jersey is crazy.


01:50:11.219 --> 01:50:12.582
You know what we do here?


01:50:12.803 --> 01:50:14.902
Cops arrest bad guys.


01:50:16.744 --> 01:50:18.623
Before you get on that bridge again,


01:50:18.881 --> 01:50:20.355
you should call me first.


01:50:21.460 --> 01:50:22.712
To make sure it's safe.


01:50:25.512 --> 01:50:29.159
"I'm gonna enlighten some of my friends,
I can guarantee you peace of mind. "


01:50:29.343 --> 01:50:30.927
That's what you told me, Dominic.


01:50:31.959 --> 01:50:34.758
"I can guarantee you peace of mind!"


01:50:35.422 --> 01:50:37.079
I don't feel so peaceful!


01:50:42.495 --> 01:50:44.705
They tried to kill my wife!


01:50:49.126 --> 01:50:50.157
Who was that?


01:50:52.920 --> 01:50:54.541
Maybe one of your people.


01:50:55.351 --> 01:50:57.156
- I don't know yet.
- You don't?


01:50:57.746 --> 01:50:58.925
You don't know.


01:51:00.693 --> 01:51:02.645
I'll tell you what I know,
maybe I should just...


01:51:03.051 --> 01:51:04.672
put 500 guns out there on the street,


01:51:04.819 --> 01:51:06.734
start shooting up people
just to make a point.


01:51:06.882 --> 01:51:09.129
It was a junkie,
or it was a rival.


01:51:09.682 --> 01:51:11.966
Some dumb ass kid
trying to make a name for himself.


01:51:12.187 --> 01:51:13.734
Someone you forgot to pay off.


01:51:14.250 --> 01:51:16.349
Someone you slighted
without even realizing it.


01:51:17.307 --> 01:51:19.149
Could be someone
you put out of business.


01:51:19.444 --> 01:51:21.580
For being so successful.
Look at you!


01:51:22.391 --> 01:51:23.422
Success,


01:51:23.791 --> 01:51:26.627
it's got enemies.
Lots of enemies.


01:51:27.696 --> 01:51:29.427
The success took a shot at you.


01:51:29.685 --> 01:51:31.343
What you gonna do?
Kill it?


01:51:31.527 --> 01:51:33.369
You gonna become unsuccessful?


01:51:34.916 --> 01:51:37.532
We can be successful
and have enemies, right?


01:51:38.195 --> 01:51:41.179
Or be unsuccessful too,
and have friends.


01:51:42.358 --> 01:51:43.942
That's the choice we make.


01:51:45.894 --> 01:51:49.467
<i>The final evacuation of military
and diplomatic personnel</i>


01:51:49.652 --> 01:51:52.562
<i>continued throughout the night
as North Vietnamese troops</i>


01:51:52.857 --> 01:51:55.914
<i>marched on Saigon.
The imminent fall of the city</i>


01:51:56.209 --> 01:51:59.082
<i>has brought chaos
and a growing sense of desperation...</i>


01:52:08.513 --> 01:52:11.460
<i>- Operator.
- Bangkok 367, international.</i>


01:52:12.050 --> 01:52:13.376
One moment, please.


01:52:20.633 --> 01:52:21.812
<i>Sawadeekap.</i>


01:52:22.696 --> 01:52:25.017
<i>- Nate.
- Hey Frank, what's up?</i>


01:52:25.348 --> 01:52:26.675
What's going on over there?


01:52:26.859 --> 01:52:28.848
<i>- It's all over.
- Yeah, I'm watchin the news.</i>


01:52:28.995 --> 01:52:31.832
<i>- What the hell's going on?
- The game's over, Frank.</i>


01:52:32.421 --> 01:52:35.184
It's done. Everybody going home baby.
Give peace a chance.


01:52:35.368 --> 01:52:38.352
Well now, I'm not... Listen to me.
I want two thou'.


01:52:39.421 --> 01:52:42.073
I want 2,000 kis in the air.


01:52:42.257 --> 01:52:43.805
<i>It's impossible, Frank.</i>


01:52:44.173 --> 01:52:47.304
<i>- All our resources are going home.
- Tell you what. I'm on my way there.</i>


01:52:47.562 --> 01:52:48.851
<i>- Right now?
- Yeah.</i>


01:52:58.945 --> 01:53:00.382
Spear, wake the fuck up!


01:53:00.750 --> 01:53:01.782
What?


01:53:03.403 --> 01:53:06.387
- Where do you think you're goin?
- Don't hurt me, Jimmy!


01:53:08.523 --> 01:53:10.144
- Jesus, fuck!
- Police!


01:53:10.513 --> 01:53:12.428
- Drop the gun, Jimmy!
- Drop it!


01:53:12.833 --> 01:53:14.786
- Let me see your hands!
- Drop the fuckin gun!


01:53:14.970 --> 01:53:17.586
I'm not playing,
I'll blast your fuckin head!


01:53:17.807 --> 01:53:19.170
Don't shoot!


01:53:21.012 --> 01:53:22.227
I got your gun,


01:53:22.854 --> 01:53:24.290
and I got your prints.


01:53:25.432 --> 01:53:26.832
You know what you got?


01:53:27.532 --> 01:53:28.858
You got attempted murder.


01:53:29.816 --> 01:53:31.511
Eighteen fucking years!


01:53:32.100 --> 01:53:35.121
Attempted murder is the same as murder,
that’s Grand Jury.


01:53:35.563 --> 01:53:37.810
Now the Grand Jury
could come back favorably.


01:53:38.031 --> 01:53:40.647
It could be reduced to manslaughter.


01:53:41.826 --> 01:53:43.262
Maybe even self defense.


01:53:43.557 --> 01:53:45.288
Depends on how we want
to deal with you.


01:53:45.473 --> 01:53:47.167
You see where this is fucking going?


01:53:47.462 --> 01:53:48.678
Let’s say you beat it.


01:53:48.862 --> 01:53:51.072
What do you think
your cousin Frank’ll think?


01:53:51.256 --> 01:53:53.393
He'll know that at some point in time,


01:53:53.614 --> 01:53:55.787
we sat you down
and talked to you like this.


01:53:56.119 --> 01:53:58.440
And then you go to court
and you beat attempted murder?


01:53:58.845 --> 01:54:00.797
What he's gonna think?
Is he stupid?


01:54:01.018 --> 01:54:03.671
- Is your cousin Frank stupid?
- Answer him!


01:54:04.592 --> 01:54:07.060
No, he's gonna assume that you talked.


01:54:10.302 --> 01:54:12.291
But right now, Frank doesn't know.


01:54:12.991 --> 01:54:15.091
You want Frank
to read this in the papers?


01:54:15.349 --> 01:54:17.117
Or you just wanna walk out of here?


01:54:17.375 --> 01:54:19.069
No bail, no trial,


01:54:19.254 --> 01:54:21.280
no jail,
just walk out of here today.


01:54:22.201 --> 01:54:23.380
Your choice.


01:54:33.842 --> 01:54:36.347
Opium plants are hearty enough


01:54:36.531 --> 01:54:38.373
to outlive any war.


01:54:39.294 --> 01:54:42.904
They’ll still be here
long after the troops are gone.


01:54:44.746 --> 01:54:46.846
What are you going to do
for transportation


01:54:47.141 --> 01:54:49.277
when the last US plane goes home?


01:54:50.051 --> 01:54:51.524
I'll figure something out.


01:54:53.587 --> 01:54:55.798
You’ll see me again,
that's for sure.


01:54:57.603 --> 01:55:00.366
It’s not in my best interest
to say this, Frank...


01:55:01.139 --> 01:55:03.571
but quitting while you’re ahead


01:55:04.749 --> 01:55:06.444
is not the same as quitting.


01:55:50.098 --> 01:55:51.056
Go get him.


01:55:54.187 --> 01:55:56.213
- Whenever you want to, baby.
- A second.


01:55:56.692 --> 01:55:57.760
It's Frank.


01:56:01.960 --> 01:56:03.065
Newark.


01:56:04.097 --> 01:56:05.312
short-term


01:56:06.344 --> 01:56:07.817
parking lot 3.


01:56:08.701 --> 01:56:09.954
Short-term lot 3.


01:56:10.470 --> 01:56:12.054
It is the Mustang, right?


01:56:12.349 --> 01:56:13.675
OK, what's the plate number?


01:56:14.043 --> 01:56:15.038
K


01:56:15.259 --> 01:56:16.290
- A.
- KA.


01:56:16.585 --> 01:56:17.874
<i>76</i>


01:56:18.022 --> 01:56:19.090
<i>0</i>


01:56:19.422 --> 01:56:20.453
<i>All right.</i>


01:56:21.706 --> 01:56:23.584
There's no short-term lot 3 in Newark.


01:56:23.879 --> 01:56:26.089
- They got letters, A, B,C, D.
- I know!


01:56:26.384 --> 01:56:28.152
Maybe he means a time, 3 o'clock?


01:56:28.558 --> 01:56:30.326
This is no Jersey plate.


01:56:31.431 --> 01:56:32.905
Nor a New York one.


01:56:33.420 --> 01:56:35.925
KA 760.


01:56:37.436 --> 01:56:38.541
Kilo Alpha?


01:56:39.609 --> 01:56:40.935
A plane tail number?


01:56:41.635 --> 01:56:43.035
Kilo Alpha 760.


01:56:44.619 --> 01:56:47.345
You check commercial planes,
you guys private planes.


01:56:47.603 --> 01:56:49.040
Everything, from a little Cessna


01:56:49.261 --> 01:56:51.140
to the biggest fuckin jet, alright?


01:56:51.434 --> 01:56:53.829
Check the miltary planes.
Where you going? Stay there.


01:56:54.050 --> 01:56:55.229
Sit down!


01:57:18.548 --> 01:57:19.616
Captain?


01:57:20.353 --> 01:57:22.489
Richie Roberts, Essex County.


01:57:22.895 --> 01:57:24.442
I know you're expecting us.


01:57:24.700 --> 01:57:25.805
Here's our warrant.


01:57:26.173 --> 01:57:27.573
We're looking on the plane.


01:57:27.831 --> 01:57:29.710
- Wait.
- Scotty, stop all these soldiers,


01:57:29.894 --> 01:57:31.662
check their bags, everyone of'em.


01:57:42.235 --> 01:57:43.672
No knock, warrant.


01:57:44.851 --> 01:57:46.324
Go ahead, start upstairs.


01:57:46.619 --> 01:57:48.498
- Where are they going?
- Step this way.


01:57:49.492 --> 01:57:50.818
M'am, please sit down.


01:57:51.113 --> 01:57:52.218
What is this?


01:57:54.171 --> 01:57:55.350
Hold it! Stop!


01:57:56.749 --> 01:57:59.512
Nothing leaves this area, all right?
Slow down with this.


01:58:00.175 --> 01:58:02.091
- Stop these trucks.
- Hold on.


01:58:02.312 --> 01:58:04.154
Everything off the walls,
pull it all down.


01:58:04.301 --> 01:58:05.480
That thing's a monster.


01:58:05.628 --> 01:58:07.801
- What is this?
- Nothing goes out til we've checked it.


01:58:07.985 --> 01:58:09.348
All right, Captain? Nothing.


01:58:09.533 --> 01:58:11.595
We're gonna take the plane down,
look at the trucks.


01:58:11.743 --> 01:58:14.322
Every man here gets searched.
Read the warrant, Sir.


01:58:15.464 --> 01:58:17.821
Your husband’s
illustrious career is over.


01:58:18.890 --> 01:58:21.873
The Feds are going to come in
and take everything.


01:58:22.352 --> 01:58:23.752
They gonna take it all.


01:58:24.010 --> 01:58:25.963
But not before I get my gratuity.


01:58:27.289 --> 01:58:28.504
So, where’s the money?


01:58:28.762 --> 01:58:30.089
What money?


01:58:30.383 --> 01:58:31.746
What money, you ask?


01:58:32.188 --> 01:58:33.367
The getaway money


01:58:33.588 --> 01:58:36.204
that Frank and every other gangster
keeps in his house.


01:58:36.462 --> 01:58:39.335
If you leave now, there's a chance
Frank might not kill you.


01:58:41.509 --> 01:58:42.872
Shut up! Sit down!


01:58:43.277 --> 01:58:44.345
Sit down!


01:59:26.710 --> 01:59:30.836
<i>...plan the evacuation of all remaining
US combat forces from Vietnam.</i>


01:59:31.204 --> 01:59:33.635
<i>News that come too late for some,</i>


01:59:33.856 --> 01:59:36.877
<i>as here on the solemn tarmac
at Dover Air Force Base,</i>


01:59:37.356 --> 01:59:40.782
<i>this C-130 loaded down
with its sorrowful cargo,</i>


01:59:41.114 --> 01:59:43.213
<i>a cargo of America's bravest and best,</i>


01:59:43.361 --> 01:59:45.240
<i>en route to their final resting places.</i>


02:00:00.749 --> 02:00:02.185
You guys, take this coffin down.


02:00:10.806 --> 02:00:12.684
- Open it.
- I'm not doing that.


02:00:19.242 --> 02:00:21.231
Great barking dog, huh?


02:00:29.335 --> 02:00:30.846
You stop this. Right now!


02:00:31.214 --> 02:00:33.903
My warrant gives me permission
to examine this plane.


02:00:35.524 --> 02:00:36.924
The plane and its cargo.


02:00:37.403 --> 02:00:39.208
But you don't have my permission.


02:00:40.534 --> 02:00:41.934
I don't need it, Captain.


02:00:43.629 --> 02:00:44.955
Easy! Easy!


02:00:48.676 --> 02:00:49.965
Move out of the way.


02:00:56.301 --> 02:00:57.333
Damn!


02:01:02.453 --> 02:01:03.522
That's enough!


02:01:11.295 --> 02:01:13.468
Stay with the coffins.
Don't let'em out of your sight.


02:01:13.616 --> 02:01:14.721
Got it.


02:01:16.857 --> 02:01:18.257
Help me out with this.


02:01:43.087 --> 02:01:45.186
That was a military transport plane.


02:01:45.592 --> 02:01:48.207
If there was heroin onboard,
someone in the military would have


02:01:48.355 --> 02:01:50.860
to be involved, which means
that even as it fights a war


02:01:51.154 --> 02:01:53.254
that's claimed 50,000 American lives,


02:01:53.696 --> 02:01:55.685
the military is smuggling narcotics.


02:01:55.833 --> 02:01:58.375
That is how this event today
will be interpreted.


02:01:58.927 --> 02:02:01.764
That someone employed by this Office
believes that the US Army


02:02:01.911 --> 02:02:03.458
is in the drug trafficking business,


02:02:04.453 --> 02:02:06.553
and is trying to prove it
by desecrating the remains


02:02:06.774 --> 02:02:10.568
of young men who've given their lives
in the defense of democracy!


02:02:10.826 --> 02:02:13.000
- There's dope on that plane.
- Shut the fuck up!


02:02:14.436 --> 02:02:15.726
Is it any wonder then,


02:02:15.984 --> 02:02:17.494
because of your actions,


02:02:17.973 --> 02:02:20.883
the entire federal narcotics program
is now in jeopardy of being dismantled


02:02:21.141 --> 02:02:23.241
as completely and enthusiastically


02:02:23.388 --> 02:02:25.230
as that fucking transport plane?


02:02:25.377 --> 02:02:27.698
That’s what you’ve accomplished
Mr. Roberts. Single-handedly.


02:02:27.919 --> 02:02:29.393
I had good information


02:02:29.982 --> 02:02:33.298
the target of my investigation
was bringing dope in on that plane.


02:02:33.740 --> 02:02:35.471
- And that target is?
- Frank Lucas.


02:02:35.619 --> 02:02:37.571
- Who?
- His name is Frank Lucas.


02:02:37.903 --> 02:02:40.408
Who's Frank Lucas? Who's he work for?
Which family?


02:02:40.555 --> 02:02:42.176
He's not Italian. He's black.


02:02:45.897 --> 02:02:48.144
Is that supposed to be
some kind of a joke?


02:02:48.807 --> 02:02:51.312
You’re this close to the end
of your career in law enforcement


02:02:51.422 --> 02:02:52.712
and you’re making jokes?


02:02:53.927 --> 02:02:55.548
My investigation indicates


02:02:56.322 --> 02:02:59.269
that Frank Lucas is above the mafia
in the dope business.


02:02:59.822 --> 02:03:02.364
My investigation also
indicates that Frank Lucas


02:03:02.658 --> 02:03:05.532
buys direct from a source
in Southeast Asia,


02:03:05.826 --> 02:03:08.994
he cuts out the middlemen,
and uses US military planes


02:03:09.252 --> 02:03:11.794
and personnel to transport pure No. 4


02:03:12.089 --> 02:03:14.262
heroin into the United States,
and he's been doing so,


02:03:14.373 --> 02:03:16.915
on a regular basis, since 1969!


02:03:17.136 --> 02:03:18.904
I have cases against every member


02:03:19.125 --> 02:03:20.857
- of his organization.
- His organization?


02:03:21.041 --> 02:03:23.877
No fucking nigger has accomplished what
the American Mafia hasn’t


02:03:24.098 --> 02:03:25.130
in a hundred years!


02:03:25.314 --> 02:03:26.530
And you'd know that how?


02:03:26.677 --> 02:03:28.556
Cause your head is stuck up
your fuckin ass?


02:03:28.851 --> 02:03:31.024
Lou, do me a favor,
get this fucking kike out of here.


02:03:31.724 --> 02:03:32.755
Kike?


02:03:39.571 --> 02:03:40.749
Make it stick.


02:03:41.634 --> 02:03:44.028
Spearman's with the coffins,
about a quarter mile away.


02:04:15.231 --> 02:04:16.262
Doctor!


02:04:18.399 --> 02:04:19.430
What?


02:04:20.130 --> 02:04:23.003
Fucking Trupo came by the house.
It's bad.


02:04:39.213 --> 02:04:41.202
I need to speak with you
a minute, please.


02:04:41.423 --> 02:04:43.559
- Sit down just a minute.
- I have to go.


02:04:44.149 --> 02:04:45.917
Would you come back a little later?


02:04:46.838 --> 02:04:48.238
- Thank you.
- Ma, I gotta go.


02:04:48.385 --> 02:04:51.075
- Just a few words.
- Listen to me, I got...


02:04:51.259 --> 02:04:53.432
Please sit down.
Just a few words.


02:04:53.985 --> 02:04:55.864
I've been thinking about some things.


02:04:56.122 --> 02:04:57.742
If you had been a preacher,


02:04:57.927 --> 02:04:59.769
